{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg -n '\"'^##|'\"\\\\bD(702|703|704|705|711|719|720)\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -70\"","aggregated_output":"     201 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\n9116:## D655 · 2026-11-17 · Council consensus (D439, D654): send the paired test of the narrow passage v5.5 on astra, shared cap $3.60\n9158:## D656 · 2026-11-17 · The paired test of v5.5 (D655): FAIL by the prewritten rule; D654's class recovered on the exposed targets; v5.5 kept as an unaccepted candidate; next, a $0 census of the listing defect\n9197:## D657 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: cost is set aside until the new system works\n9208:## D658 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: a new reference for the final-answer test's control line, written for the questions the new system asks\n9229:## D659 · 2026-11-17 · Correction of D658's material line; the new reference's design, version 2, goes to council round 2\n9249:## D660 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: three rules of the new control-line reference, chosen after the orchestrator had seen the stored judgements; D658's option text recorded word for word\n9273:## D661 · 2026-11-17 · Open defect: the Codex-family blind readers ran with Codex memories on, which carry project context\n9293:## D662 · 2026-11-17 · Reflection council 9 (Alex's request): the work drifted from D560's agreed way out; hold the listed work and put Deck 1 to Alex first (council consensus)\n9353:## D663 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: the council marks Deck 1 instead of him; it passes the instrument checks; next, the product comparison's design\n9383:## D664 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: no budget needed for the comparison; D658 waits; the council determines whether the six lines still make sense and what decides readiness\n9398:## D665 · 2026-11-17 · Council (D664, Alex's \"run your council to determine\"): the six lines stop blocking release; one product comparison against the running pipeline decides readiness, its verdict written before the first send (council consensus)\n9443:## D666 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: write a run plan for the release comparison, monitor it carefully, no scope drift\n9460:## D667 · 2026-11-17 · Under D666 and D439 (council, run-plan rounds 1–10): the release comparison's run plan and the rules it takes for this run\n9519:## D668 · 2026-11-17 · Under D667 (council): the old replays are all reads; the scored window is 08-31 to 09-20; every kept article in it is read for the census\n9545:## D669 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: score on 09-07 to 09-20, excluding only articles a system processed or a reader read\n9570:## D670 · 2026-11-17 · Under D669 (council check): 410 of the 502 articles of 09-07 to 09-20 are kept and frozen\n9589:## D671 · 2026-11-17 · Under D667 and D668 (council): the blind matter list is frozen at N = 32\n9618:## D672 · 2026-11-17 · Alex's \"开始跑\" with the stage-0 freeze review: the slice goes ahead; the scorer and cards are built during the run against a rule frozen to the last choice\n9645:## D673 · 2026-11-17 · Under D672: the card's blinding rule covers the form, not the system's own wording (before any output)\n9659:## D674 · 2026-11-17 · Alex's goal for the comparison: run, and keep tackling until the set criteria pass\n9674:## D675 · 2026-11-18 · Under D672: the reading tools' review found them not ready; fixed, and the frozen rule's open readings written down (before any output)\n10007:## D676 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison: the new system loses for two known mechanisms; keep the old system; the outcome was computable before the run (council consensus)\n10042:## D677 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison's goal loop is closed; the old system stays; no paid work continues (council consensus, D439/D544)\n10061:## D678 · 2026-11-19 · Merge design (council consensus): the old system opens questions, the clean system reads and organises evidence, the same judge answers; a 12-article test awaits Alex's approval\n10079:## D679 · 2026-11-19 · Alex lifts D677's paid-send stop for the merge test only; the test runs on 70 articles, two old draws, two judging arms, under a $5 ledger\n10102:## D680 · 2026-11-19 · Merge test closed (council e): delivery verified, the registered test did not pass (P2's proxy clause and V missed)\n10125:## D681 · 2026-11-20 · Alex opens the hybrid system's build and test; phase 1 is a new judge version (J2) for the judge's reasoning errors\n10150:## D682 · 2026-11-20 · Under D681 (council): J2a and J2b retired; the carried previous conclusion is the lead mechanism; a separating test on complete evidence\n10177:## D683 · 2026-11-20 · Under D681/D682 (council H): the removal of the previous conclusion is not accepted; one presentation-only test goes to Alex\n10199:## D684 · 2026-11-20 · Under D683: Alex approves the presentation-only test and hands the iteration to Claude (\"那你自己持续迭代\")\n10212:## D685 · 2026-11-20 · Under D684 (councils I–K): the fresh test cannot be fed; H1 fails its diagnostic; the judge line pauses within D198; phase 2 (opening) starts\n10240:## D686 · 2026-11-20 · Under D685 (council L): the opening census; D382 goes to Alex first\n10263:## D687 · 2026-11-20 · Alex: in the hybrid, a company's own material figure gets its own question\n10274:## D688 · 2026-11-20 · Under D687 (council M): no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone; to Alex, keep old and pause the hybrid's release line\n10308:## D689 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses option 1 (keep old, pause the hybrid's release line); council N closes the judge and c8 lines for now\n10360:## D690 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A: poc-v118 is the product, the research line rests until his new direction; the D681–D689 records are committed locally\n10375:## D691 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A after council Q: no daily wrapper yet; link related questions first, a $0 check then a few cents\n10398:## D692 · 2026-11-20 · Under Alex's A (D691): the dependency probe passes its registered rule; the dependency design review reopens at $0\n10414:## D693 · 2026-11-21 · Under Alex's A (D691): the design for linking related questions reaches council consensus at $0; three choices go to Alex before any build or send; the self-made reference is traced\n10439:## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n10454:## D695 · 2026-11-21 · Alex narrows the first linking version to number questions, one of them newly opened\n10467:## D696 · 2026-11-21 · Alex keeps the July test's $0.15 limit as a reservation stop priced from each request's size\n10482:## D697 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the $0 proof of the linking version; the July comparison is sent (D694 (c), D696)\n10493:## D698 · 2026-11-21 · The July test of the linking version passes its frozen rule; next steps go to Alex\n10505:## D699 · 2026-11-21 · Alex continues with A: the whole-window measurement of the linking version, designed with the council at $0 first\n10515:## D700 · 2026-11-21 · Alex approves a $0.10 ceiling for the census of the link decisions before the whole-window run\n10525:## D701 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the census harness (rounds 13–16); the census of link decisions is sent under D700\n10541:## D702 · 2026-11-21 · The census of link decisions passes its registered gate; council R: probe a sharpened link question before buying judgements\n10556:## D703 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses to probe a sharpened link question before the paid run\n10558:- **The question** (after D702): \"连题统计通过了事先定的关 … 问题是它在'部分读整体'和'整体读部分'之间拿不定主意，而且有一条很可能连反了 … 下一步怎么走？\"\n10567:## D704 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the version-2 link question for its probe (rounds 18–19); the probe is sent under D703\n10573:  this probe tests under D703; D537 decided only the Data Center case.\n10583:## D705 · 2026-11-21 · The version-2 link question passes its registered gate; council R: version 2 goes to the paid design\n10594:## D706 · 2026-11-21 · poc-v120 (link questions version 2) passes council review as a product configuration; the paid design needs four changes\n10611:## D707 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the paid design (version 6, rounds 22–27) for building its harness\n10625:## D708 · 2026-11-21 · Council R (reflection, round 31): a one-pair pilot before the full paid comparison\n10641:## D709 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the pilot of the paid comparison (rounds 32–36); the send waits for Alex's ceiling\n10652:## D710 · 2026-11-21 · Alex approves a $2.50 ceiling for the pilot; pair 1 is sent\n10660:## D711 · 2026-11-21 · Pilot pair 1 is inconclusive (control double refusal); the comparison is closed; council round 37 recommends a citation-only judge version to Alex\n10686:    `other`, and the direction is a judgement, which D704 left open on purpose.\n10689:## D712 · 2026-11-21 · Alex opens a citation-only judge version (closed per-request id lists), tested at $0 first\n10696:- **Scope:** a new judge version whose only change is the answer format's id fields (D711's recommendation). The link direction stays\n10699:## D713 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the citation-only judge design (round 38, four passes); build judging-v12 and poc-v121 with the $0 test\n10721:## D714 · 2026-11-21 · judging-v12 and poc-v121 built; every registered $0 check passes; the paid acceptance step is Alex's\n10756:## D715 · 2026-11-22 · Alex approves $0.50 for the paid acceptance step of judging-v12\n10765:## D716 · 2026-11-22 · Council R passes the paid acceptance probe's design (round 40, six passes); the harness and its $0 rehearsal next\n10783:## D717 · 2026-11-22 · Council R passes the probe harness and its $0 rehearsal (round 41, five passes); the paid probe is sent at Alex's $0.50\n10799:## D718 · 2026-11-22 · The paid acceptance probe of judging-v12: registered verdict NOT READY; Council B recommends keeping poc-v118\n10825:## D719 · 2026-11-22 · Alex stops the citation line: judging-v12 is not adopted; poc-v118 stays the product\n10837:  - The link-direction design (D711) and the citation follow-up are not started. No further spend.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
