ales guidance is the reference and sits at rung 2 ($20 billion to less than $25 billion).|Roughly $25 billion or more for FY2027: carry forward the approximately $20 billion Vera standalone forecast and add Grace’s reported trailing-12-month CPU revenue above $5 billion as a run-rate.\n7520|2026-09-09|1|NVIDIA’s roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone Vera CPU sales guidance is the market/company reference and sits at rung 2 ($20 billion to less than $25 billion).|Roughly $20 billion of FY2027 standalone Vera CPU revenue plus Grace CPU revenue at a run-rate above $5 billion (reported on a trailing-12-month basis) implies total CPU revenue above $25 billion, placing the forecast in rung 1.\n7758|2026-09-10|1|NVIDIA’s roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone CPU sales guidance is the market/company reference and sits in rung 2 ($20 billion to less than $25 billion).|More than $25 billion: approximately $20 billion of guided FY2027 standalone Vera CPU revenue, plus Grace CPU revenue whose trailing-12-month figure already exceeded $5 billion and is carried forward as a run-rate.\n7911|2026-09-11|1|NVIDIA’s roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone-CPU outlook is the reference; it sits in rung 2 ($20 billion to less than $25 billion).|Carry Grace’s reported more-than-$5-billion trailing-12-month revenue run-rate into FY2027 and add it to the roughly $20 billion standalone-CPU outlook, implying total CPU revenue around or above $25 billion. This reaches the rung 1 boundary.\n8050|2026-09-12|1|NVIDIA’s roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone-CPU outlook is the relevant reference; it sits at rung 2 ($20 billion to less than $25 billion).|About $25 billion or more: carry the reported Grace CPU trailing-12-month revenue of more than $5 billion forward as a run-rate into FY2027 and add it to the roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone-CPU outlook. This reaches rung 1’s $25 billion minimum.\n8141|2026-09-13|1|NVIDIA's roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone-CPU outlook is the reference; it si