27 revenue of $81.615 billion and guided Q2 revenue of $91.0 billion, then carry the stated 11% sequential growth rate forward to Q3 ($101.0 billion) and Q4 ($112.1 billion).\n8786|2026-07-25|3|Bloomberg's FY2027 revenue estimate of $393 billion is the market reference and sits in rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).|About $385.7 billion: use reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.615 billion and Q2 guidance of $91 billion, then carry the guided 11% sequential growth forward to approximately $101.0 billion in Q3 and $112.1 billion in Q4.\n8791|2026-07-26|3|Bloomberg's $393 billion FY2027 estimate (also consistent with approximately 82% growth from FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion) is the market reference and sits in rung 3: $350 billion to less than $400 billion.|About $385.7 billion: $81.615 billion reported for Q1 plus $91 billion guided for Q2, with the guided 11% sequential growth carried forward to approximately $101.0 billion in Q3 and $112.1 billion in Q4.\n8795|2026-07-27|3|Bloomberg’s $393 billion FY2027 estimate (with reported market growth estimates of 80%–82%) is the reference and sits in rung 3.|About $385.7 billion for FY2027: $81.615 billion reported in Q1 plus $91 billion guided for Q2, followed by Q3 and Q4 estimates of about $101.0 billion and $112.1 billion by carrying the 11% sequential growth in the Q2 outlook forward.\n8799|2026-07-28|3|Bloomberg’s FY2027 revenue estimate of $393 billion is the market reference and sits in rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion). The 80% growth consensus also implies approximately $388.6 billion using FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion.|About $385.7 billion: $81.615 billion reported in Q1 plus $91 billion guided for Q2, followed by Q3 and Q4 at 11% sequential growth ($101.0 billion and $112.1 billion). This is below rung 3’s $400 billion upper boundary and above its $350 billion lower boundary.\n8803|2026-07-29|3|Bloomberg’s FY2027 estimate of $393 billion and the cited 80%–82% growth expectations 