lion; this is rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).|Q1 and Q2 reported revenue sum to $177.8 billion; adding Q3 guidance of $108 billion and carrying its approximately 12% sequential growth forward implies Q4 revenue of about $121.3 billion. The resulting FY2027 total is approximately $407.1 billion.\n8959|2026-09-05|2|LSEG analysts' $396 billion FY2027 revenue expectation; rung 3 (Neutral: $350 billion to less than $400 billion).|The first two reported quarters total $177.8 billion. Add Q3's $108 billion midpoint guidance and carry its roughly 12.3% sequential growth into Q4 ($108 billion × 1.123 ≈ $121.3 billion), implying approximately $407.1 billion for FY2027.\n8963|2026-09-06|2|The latest stated Wall Street expectation is approximately $411 billion for FY2027 (e4097), which sits at rung 2; the earlier LSEG estimate of $396 billion (e2421) sits at rung 3.|Q1 and Q2 reported revenue total $177.8 billion; adding Q3 guidance of $108 billion and carrying the 12.3% sequential growth rate into Q4 implies about $121.3 billion for Q4 and approximately $407.1 billion for FY2027.\n8968|2026-09-07|2|Latest cited Wall Street FY2027 revenue expectation: about $411 billion, rung 2 ($400 billion to less than $450 billion). The earlier LSEG estimate of $396 billion is rung 3.|Approximately $407.1 billion: reported Q1 and Q2 revenue of $81.6 billion and $96.2 billion, plus Q3 midpoint guidance of $108 billion, total $285.8 billion; carrying roughly 12.3% sequential growth forward gives Q4 of about $121.3 billion.\n8973|2026-09-08|2|The latest stated Wall Street expectation is about $411 billion, which sits in rung 2 ($400 billion to less than $450 billion); the earlier LSEG expectation of $396 billion sits in rung 3.|Q1 and Q2 actual revenue total $177.8 billion; adding Q3 midpoint guidance of $108 billion gives $285.8 billion through Q3. Carrying the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance forward gives Q4 of about $121.3 billion and FY2027 total reve