, Q3 guidance of $108 billion, and Q4 estimated by carrying Q3’s roughly 12% sequential growth forward ($121 billion) imply approximately $407 billion for FY2027.\n9002|2026-09-15|2|Wall Street analysts’ $411 billion FY2027 estimate is in rung 2. Zacks’ 87.4% FY2027 growth estimate applied to approximately $215.9 billion of FY2026 revenue implies about $405 billion, also in rung 2.|About $418 billion: add reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion to a Q3 estimate of roughly $113.5 billion (the midpoint of the $113–$114 billion forecast, supported by the reported guidance-beat history), then carry the 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance into Q4, giving about $127 billion.\n9006|2026-09-16|2|Analysts’ FY2027 revenue expectation of about $411 billion is the market reference and sits in rung 2. Zacks’ 87.4% growth estimate applied to FY2026 revenue of about $215.9 billion implies about $405 billion, also rung 2.|About $419 billion: Q1 and Q2 actual revenue totals $177.8 billion; applying the 3.1% average beat to the high end of Q3 guidance implies about $113.6 billion for Q3, and carrying the guide’s 12% sequential growth into Q4 implies about $127.2 billion. This falls within rung 2’s $400–450 billion range.\n9010|2026-09-17|2|Analysts’ $411 billion FY2027 revenue estimate is the market reference and sits in rung 2; Zacks’ 87.4% growth estimate on FY2026 revenue implies about $405 billion, also rung 2.|About $419 billion: Q1 and Q2 total $177.8 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $113.6 billion by applying the 3.1% average beat to the high end of guidance, and Q4 at about $127.2 billion by carrying forward the guided 12% sequential growth.\n9014|2026-09-18|2|The market reference is the $411 billion FY2027 analyst expectation, which sits in rung 2. Zacks’ 87.4% revenue-growth consensus implies about $404.5 billion from FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion, also rung 2.|About $418.5 billion, or roughly $419 billion: Q1 and Q2 reported revenue totals $177.8 billion; the Q3 estimate is about $113.5 billion; carrying the guided 12% sequential growth into Q4 implies about $127.1 billion.\n9018|2026-09-19|2|Analyst expectations of about $411 billion (e4061, e4097) are the market reference and sit at rung 2. Zacks' 87.4% FY2027 growth estimate implies about $404.5 billion from the reported FY2026 base of approximately $215.9 billion, also rung 2.|About $419 billion: Q1 and Q2 total $177.8 billion; applying the historical average 3.1% beat above the $110.16 billion high end of Q3 guidance implies about $113.6 billion for Q3, and carrying the guided 12% sequential growth forward implies about $127.2 billion for Q4. The sum is approximately $418.6 billion.\n9023|2026-09-20|2|Wall Street analysts expect about $411 billion of FY2027 revenue (rung 2). Zacks’ 87.4% growth estimate against FY2026 revenue of about $215.9 billion implies about $404.5 billion, also rung 2.|About $419 billion: Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion plus Q2’s $96.2 billion, an estimated Q3 of about $113.6 billion (the $110.16 billion high end of guidance adjusted by the reported 3.1% average beat), and Q4 of about $127.5 billion by carrying forward roughly 12% sequential growth.\nlinked-1 v9 71 ('How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?',) [(1, 'Strongly bullish', 450000000000.0, None), (2, 'Bullish', 400000000000.0, 450000000000.0), (3, 'Neutral', 350000000000.0, 400000000000.0), (4, 'Bearish', 300000000000.0, 350000000000.0), (5, 'Strongly bearish', None, 300000000000.0)]\nrange (8744, '2026-07-10', 3) (9024, '2026-09-20', 3)\n8744|2026-07-10|3|No direct FY2027 Data Center market consensus is supplied. The best supplied proxy is Bloomberg's $393 billion FY2027 total-revenue expectation in v14, which is rung 3 for total revenue; at NVIDIA's Q1 Data Center share of 92%, it implies about $362 billion of Data Center revenue, rung 3.|About $356 billion: carrying the approximately 11.5% sequential increase from Q1 total revenue of $81.6 billion to Q2 guidance of $91 billion forward gives roughly $387 billion of FY2027 total revenue, then applying the Q1 Data Center mix of 92% gives roughly $356 billion. This is a run-rate estimate, not a flat annualization of Q1.\n8747|2026-07-12|3|No direct FY2027 Data Center consensus is supplied. The Bloomberg FY2027 total-revenue reference is $393 billion; applying the reported Q1 Data Center share of 92% gives a proxy of about $362 billion, in rung 3.|About $356 billion: v14's approximately $387 billion FY2027 total-revenue run-rate, derived by carrying the Q1-to-Q2 guided sequential growth pace forward, multiplied by the reported 92% Q1 Data Center share.\n8751|2026-07-13|3|Bloomberg’s $393 billion FY2027 total-revenue projection, translated using the 92% Data Center mix, implies about $362 billion for Data Center; that reference sits in rung 3.|Approximately $356 billion for FY2027. Starting from Q1 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, applying the Q1 92% mix to the $91 billion Q2 total-revenue guide estimates Q2 Data Center revenue at about $83.7 billion; carrying the roughly 11.5% sequential total-revenue growth rate forward gives about $93.3 billion in Q3 and $104.1 billion in Q4.\n8753|2026-07-14|3|Bloomberg's $393 billion FY2027 total-revenue projection, translated using NVIDIA's latest reported 92% Data Center share, implies about $362 billion of Data Center revenue. That reference is in rung 3 ($350 billion to below $400 billion).|About $356 billion for FY2027: dependency v14's approximately $387 billion total-revenue run-rate forecast, derived by carrying forward the sequential growth implied by Q1 actual revenue and Q2 guidance, multiplied by the reported Q1 Data Center mix of about 92%.\n8758|2026-07-15|3|Bloomberg’s FY2027 total-revenue projection of $393 billion, translated using the latest 92% Data Center mix to approximately $362 billion; this is rung 3.|Approximately $356 billion for FY2027 Data Center revenue: carry the sequential growth from Q1 total revenue of $81.6 billion to the $91 billion Q2 guide into Q3 and Q4, producing about $387 billion of FY2027 total revenue, then apply the observed 92% Data Center mix. This is below $400 billion and consistent with v14’s higher total forecast because its approximately $19.5 billion stand-alone CPU contribution is outside Data Center.\n8761|2026-07-16|3|Bloomberg’s $393 billion FY2027 total-revenue projection, converted using the latest 92% Data Center mix, implies about $361 billion of Data Center revenue and sits in rung 3.|About $376 billion: carrying the $81.6 billion Q1 result and $91 billion Q2 total-revenue guide forward implies roughly $387 billion for FY2027; applying the 92% Data Center mix gives about $356 billion, then adding v14’s approximately $19.5 billion stand-alone CPU forecast as incremental Data Center revenue gives about $376 billion.\n8765|2026-07-17|3|Bloomberg’s $393 billion FY2027 total-revenue projection, translated at the 92% Data Center mix, implies about $362 billion of Data Center revenue and sits in rung 3.|About $375 billion: the $91 billion Q2 total-revenue guide versus $81.6 billion in Q1 implies roughly 11.5% sequential growth; carrying that through Q3 and Q4 gives about $387 billion for FY2027. Applying the 92% Data Center mix gives about $356 billion, and adding v14’s approximately $19 billion stand-alone CPU estimate yields about $375 billion.\n8768|2026-07-18|3|Bloomberg’s $393 billion FY2027 total-revenue projection, translated at the latest 92% Data Center mix, implies about $362 billion of Data Center revenue and sits in rung 3.|About $375 billion for FY2027 Data Center revenue: the Q2 $91 billion total-revenue guide carried forward at the Q1-to-Q2 sequential growth rate implies roughly $387 billion for FY2027; applying the 92% Data Center mix gives about $356 billion, then adding v14’s approximately $19 billion stand-alone CPU estimate gives about $375 billion.\n8769|2026-07-19|3|Bloomberg’s $393 billion FY2027 total-revenue projection, translated at the latest 92% Data Center mix to about $362 billion; that reference sits in rung 3.|About $375 billion of FY2027 Data Center revenue: v14’s approximately $406 billion total-revenue forecast, multiplied by the latest 92% Data Center mix, implies roughly $374 billion, rounded to about $375 billion. Noetra’s 140MW plan scales to roughly $6.9 billion at $49 billion/GW, but its unspecified delivery timing and planned Rubin deployment warrant discounting rather than adding the full amount.\n8772|2026-07-20|3|Bloomberg's FY2027 total-revenue projection of $393 billion, translated using the latest roughly 92% Data Center mix, implies about $362 billion of Data Center revenue and sits in rung 3.|About $360 billion for FY2027: the current v14 forecast of approximately $387 billion total revenue multiplied by the reported 92.2% Q1 Data Center share gives about $357 billion; a modest increase to roughly 93% for management's unquantified Q2 Data Center growth acceleration gives about $360 billion.\n8775|2026-07-21|3|Bloomberg's FY2027 total-revenue projection of $393 billion is the market reference; applying the reported Q1 Data Center mix of about 92.2% implies roughly $362 billion of Data Center revenue, which is rung 3.|About $356 billion: dependency v14 forecasts approximately $387 billion of FY2027 total revenue, and applying an estimated roughly 92% Data Center share gives about $356 billion.\n8778|2026-07-22|3|Bloomberg’s FY2027 total-revenue estimate of $393 billion, translated using NVIDIA’s roughly 92% Q1 Data Center mix, implies about $362 billion of Data Center revenue and sits in rung 3.|About $352 billion: v14’s approximately $387.3 billion FY2027 total-revenue forecast multiplied by an estimated 91% Data Center share, between the reported 92% Q1 mix and the around-90% FY2027/FY2028 estimate.\n8782|2026-07-23|4|Bloomberg’s FY2027 NVIDIA total-revenue estimate is $393 billion. Applying the reported 92% Q1 Data Cent