ter.\n8907|2026-08-23|1|Wall Street's 42% FY2027 revenue-growth estimate, which is rung 3.|About $389–400 billion of FY2027 revenue: 80% growth under Morningstar's model, rising to about 85% if revenue reaches roughly $400 billion, against FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion.\n8913|2026-08-24|1|Wall Street's 42% FY2027 revenue-growth estimate is the market reference and sits in rung 3 (Neutral).|About 80–85% FY2027 revenue growth, or approximately $389–400 billion of revenue: Morningstar models 80%, while the roughly $400 billion FY2027 estimate is about 85% above FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion. Q2 guidance and the Q3 estimate support this annual outlook without treating one quarter's growth as a flat full-year run-rate.\n8917|2026-08-25|1|The ladder cites Wall Street’s 42% FY2027 estimate, which is rung 3. The more current explicit market reference is LSEG’s 83% estimate ($396 billion), which is rung 1.|About 83% FY2027 revenue growth: the LSEG estimate of $396 billion against reported FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion implies approximately 83.4%. Morningstar’s 80% model and the strong quarterly guide/estimates are consistent checks, not annualized quarterly growth rates.\n8922|2026-08-26|1|LSEG’s $396 billion FY2027 revenue estimate, equivalent to 83% growth, is the current quantified market reference and sits at rung 1. The older 42% Wall Street estimate sits at rung 3.|About $407.1 billion of FY2027 revenue, or approximately 88.5% growth versus FY2026’s $215.94 billion: $81.6 billion reported in Q1 plus $96.2 billion reported in Q2 plus $108.0 billion guided for Q3, with Q4 estimated at about $121.3 billion by carrying forward Q3’s roughly 12.3% sequential growth.\n8926|2026-08-27|1|Latest stated market reference: LSEG estimates FY2027 revenue of $396 billion, about 83% growth over FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion; that is rung 1. The older 42% Wall Street estimate is rung 3.|Q1 and Q2 revenue total $177.8 billion; adding guided Q3 revenue of $108.0 billion an