mate of 85.4% is also in rung 1.|About 70% FY2027 revenue growth: applying the CFO's full-year outlook to FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion implies about $367.1 billion in FY2027 revenue. After $81.6 billion in Q1, $96.2 billion in Q2, and the $108 billion Q3 guide, that annual outcome implies about $81.3 billion in Q4.\n8954|2026-09-03|1|LSEG expects $396 billion of FY2027 revenue, about 83% growth on FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion; this is rung 1. Zacks' 85.4% growth estimate is likewise rung 1.|Approximately $404 billion of FY2027 revenue, or about 87% growth: Q1 and Q2 actuals plus the $108 billion Q3 guide total $285.8 billion; carrying the estimated 81% Q3 year-over-year growth into Q4 implies about $118 billion in Q4.\n8958|2026-09-04|1|The latest stated market expectations are LSEG's 83% FY2027 revenue growth to $396 billion and Zacks' 85.4%; both correspond to rung 1. The earlier 42% estimate cited in e966 corresponds to rung 3, but the later quantified estimates place the current reference at rung 1.|About $407 billion of FY2027 revenue, or roughly 88% growth versus FY2026's $215.94 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2 plus the $108 billion Q3 guidance midpoint totals $285.8 billion; carrying forward the 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance gives about $121 billion in Q4.\n8962|2026-09-05|1|LSEG analysts expect FY2027 revenue growth of 83% to $396 billion, which is rung 1; Zacks' 85.4% estimate is also rung 1. The ladder's 42% Wall Street estimate is an older, lower reference.|About $407 billion of FY2027 revenue, or approximately 88.5% growth versus FY2026's $215.94 billion. This carries forward the roughly 12% sequential growth implied by the $108 billion Q3 guidance to estimate about $121 billion for Q4; the separate 70% full-year outlook implies a lower $367 billion but still clears rung 1.\n8966|2026-09-06|1|LSEG expects 83% FY2027 revenue growth to $396 billion (rung 1); Zacks' 85.4% estimate is also rung 1.|Carry forward 