well to Rubin, Arya noted that rack pricing could increase by $2-3 million, driven by upgrades across compute, networking and software.\\n- e245 [third_party_view; uk.finance.yahoo.com, reporting Vivek Arya\\u2019s note; original source Vivek Arya, Bank of America 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Vivek Arya reported that NVIDIA\\u2019s sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice the growth in cloud capital expenditure; the comparison period is not specified.\\n    Quote: Sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capex growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e253; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e247 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported FY2027 first-quarter total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue \\u2014 an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e113, e304, e313, e349; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e254 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] BofA modeled NVIDIA retaining roughly 65%\\u201370% or more of AI capital expenditures over time, with the remainder going to ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\\n    Quote: BofA still models Nvidia holding roughly 65% to 70% plus of AI capex over time, with the rest split across ASICs, AMD and other merchant vendors.\\n- e257 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The author reports that memory companies have increased high-bandwidth memory prices tenfold over the past year as demand outpaced supply.\\n    Quote: since demand is growing faster than anyone can scale up supply, they have been able to increase prices tenfold over the past year.\\n- e258 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The author reports that the spot rental price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute peaked at around $3.20 in May 2026 and then steadily declined through 2026-07-09.\\n    Quote: In comparison, this (via the compute market Ornn ) is how the spot price for an hour of time on an Nvidia H100 GPU has changed over the last year:\\nJust like Nvidia\\u2019s stock price, there\\u2019s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\\n- e259 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The author reports that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and OpenAI have launched custom processors to reduce dependence on Nvidia, and says the chips are good enough to drive down compute prices.\\n    Quote: Google , Amazon , Microsoft , and even OpenAI have launched their own custom processors to lessen their dependence on Nvidia; even if those chips aren\\u2019t as good as the latest model from Nvidia, they\\u2019re good enough to drive down the price of compute.\\n- e261 [third_party_view; Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya, as reported by Yahoo Finance; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya ; from gnews:86c243945145ed901feb26cf 2026-07-09] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said higher memory costs could pressure NVIDIA's gross margin and custom-ASIC competition was among the concerns weighing on the company.\\n    Quote: Several concerns are fueling the sell-off, Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya wrote in a note this week. They include gross margin pressure from higher memory costs, competition from custom ASIC chips, crowded investor ownership, and unproductive use of cash in vendor financing rather than stronger buybacks/dividends.\\n- e269 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA guided to second-quarter FY2027 revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%, assuming no China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: Additionally, Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%. The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e127, e317; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e272 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management described roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across calendar 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e291 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Quanta, based on data compiled by Bloomberg ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta\\u2019s monthly sales rose to NT$385.19 billion in June 2026, more than doubling year over year; Bloomberg compiled the data.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia\\u2019s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\\n- e299 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, reporting data compiled by Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg data ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg data projects NVIDIA FY2027 profits of $228 billion and sales (total revenue) of $393 billion, up 90% and 82%, respectively.\\n    Quote: chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e234; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e300 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, reporting data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data puts NVIDIA\\u2019s server GPU market share at 97% at end-2025, up from 95% at end-2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e233; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e301 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein; original source Jeran Wittenstein 2026-07-10; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] The article reports that demand for equipment going into new data centers remains strong and that NVIDIA\\u2019s market share has hardly been dented.\\n    Quote: However, the company\\u2019s market share has hardly been dented as demand for equipment going into new data centers remains strong.\\n- e302 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein; original source Jeran Wittenstein 2026-07-10; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Alphabet and Amazon are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips, adding competition for NVIDIA in AI computing.\\n    Quote: For now, that competition \\u2014 not just from AMD and Intel but also from its biggest customers like Alphabet Inc. and Amazon.com Inc., who are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips \\u2014 is a major factor holding back Nvidia\\u2019s stock price.\\n- e303 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Wall Street consensus, as reported by Trefis ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis reports Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA revenue to grow about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA\\u2019s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\\n- e304 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis reports NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e247; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e308 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to $91 billion in total revenue for Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e112, e316; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e310 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The article reported $119 billion in NVIDIA total supply commitments and identified OpenAI, Anthropic and Meta as multi-gigawatt customers.\\n    Quote: Catalysts are already contracted . Huang told investors \\u201cAgentic AI has arrived, doing productive work, generating real value and scaling rapidly\\u201d, backed by $119 billion in total supply commitments and OpenAI, Anthropic, and Meta all named as multi-gigawatt customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e131; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e312 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] The author reported concerns that major NVIDIA clients, including Meta, are shifting toward developing in-house AI chips, a potential competitive threat to NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's stock surge comes amidst growing concerns that major clients, such as Meta, are shifting towards developing their own AI chips.\\n- e313 [fact; David Moadel; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e247, e359; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e316 [party_statement; David Moadel; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA management guided to total revenue of $91 billion for Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e308, e401, e462; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e317 [party_statement; David Moadel; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA\\u2019s Q2 FY2027 revenue outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: Notably, that outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e269, e406, e414; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e326 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.62 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e111; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e328 [party_statement; tikr.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] NVIDIA estimates that support for frontier AI models, including those built by OpenAI and Anthropic, accounts for about 20% of its business; the item gives no period.\\n    Quote: To put some numbers behind that, Nvidia estimates about 20% of its business comes from supporting frontier AI models built by companies like OpenAI and Anthropic.\\n- e329 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen estimates that enterprise-application revenue across multiple industries accounts for a low-to-mid-teens share of NVIDIA revenue; the item gives no period.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, TD Cowen estimates that Nvidia\\u2019s revenue from enterprise applications across multiple industries is in the low-to-mid-teens range.\\n- e330 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen reported that rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing; no price amount or period is specified.\\n    Quote: Rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing,\\n- e331 [fact; tikr.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported quarterly total revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, and said it was the third consecutive quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Quote: The company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e273; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e333 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source Mark Zuckerberg ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg commented on slower-than-expected progress in AI agents; the item does not provide a more specific statement or measure.\\n    Quote: Comments from Meta\\u2019s Mark Zuckerberg about slower-than-expected progress in AI agents have also added caution to the broader AI narrative.\\n- e335 [third_party_view; qz.com article author; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts, compiling estimates from TrendForce, Morgan Stanley and TSMC capacity data, estimated NVIDIA held over 90% of AI training chips and 60%\\u201375% of inference chips in 2025.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's share exceeded 90% in training in 2025. Its inference share sat between 60% and 75% over the same period, undercut by growing competition from custom silicon.\\n- e336 [third_party_view; qz.com article author; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that as of March, 1.4 million Amazon Trainium chips were deployed across three generations, including more than one million Trainium2 chips running Anthropic's Claude.\\n    Quote: As of March, 1.4 million Trainium chips were deployed across three generations, according to TechCrunch , with Anthropic's Claude running on more than one million Trainium2 chips alone.\\n- e337 [fact; qz.com article author; original source Amazon ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Amazon committed 2 GW of Trainium computing capacity to OpenAI; the item gives no commitment date or delivery period.\\n    Quote: Amazon has also committed two gigawatts of Trainium computing capacity to OpenAI, putting its chips inside two of the industry's most prominent AI labs.\\n- e338 [fact; qz.com article author; original source AMD ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] AMD's Instinct MI300 series won customers including Microsoft Azure, Meta, Dell, HPE and Lenovo.\\n    Quote: Its Instinct MI300 series has won customers including Microsoft $MSFT Azure, Meta $META , Dell $DELL , HPE, and Lenovo.\\n- e339 [third_party_view; qz.com article author; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] A December 2024 SemiAnalysis benchmark study found AMD's MI300X delivered 14% slower real-world results than NVIDIA's H100 and H200 in key training benchmarks.\\n    Quote: A December 2024 SemiAnalysis benchmark study found that AMD 's MI300X, despite higher marketed performance numbers, delivered 14% slower real-world results than Nvidia 's H100 and H200 in key training benchmarks.\\n- e340 [third_party_view; qz.com article author; original source Mizuho Securities and Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Mizuho Securities estimated NVIDIA's overall AI-chip market share at 70%\\u201395%, depending on segment; Silicon Analysts projected it would settle near 75% as the total market grows past $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's overall AI chip market share, estimated by Mizuho Securities at between 70% and 95% depending on segment, is projected by Silicon Analysts to settle near 75% as the total market expands past $200 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e439; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e341 [third_party_view; qz.com article author; original source Daniel Newman, Futurum Group ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Futurum Group analyst Daniel Newman told CNBC in November 2025 that cloud providers would keep working closely with NVIDIA and AMD because they need capacity amid insatiable demand.\\n    Quote: Daniel Newman, an analyst at the Futurum Group, told CNBC in November 2025: \\\"They want to have a little bit more control over the workloads that they build. At the same time, they're going to continue to work very closely with Nvidia , with AMD , because they also need the capacity. The demand is so insatiable.\\\"\\n- e342 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] NVIDIA revenue increased 85% during its past quarter; the item does not specify the quarter.\\n    Quote: During its past quarter, Nvidia's revenue increased at an 85% clip.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e155; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e343 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 96% in Q2; the item does not specify the year or the comparison basis.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect 96% growth during Q2.\\n- e348 [third_party_view; jpost.com; original source jpost.com 2026-07-12; from gnews:c14249088492921c802c839a 2026-07-12] Nvidia's server GPU market share was about 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's firm grip on the server GPU market showed no signs of weakening, with its market share climbing to about 97% at the end of 2025, compared to 95% the previous year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e233; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e349 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported first-quarter FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e247, e370; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e351 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management forecast approximately $91 billion in second-quarter FY2027 revenue, assuming no China Data Center sales.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e112, e373, e422, e479; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e352 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA FY2027 revenue to exceed $300 billion and earnings per share to reach $8.80.\\n    Quote: Wall Street expects Nvidia to generate well over $300 billion in fiscal 2027 revenue, while consensus earnings estimates have moved to $8.80 per share.\\n- e359 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in its most recent fiscal quarter, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially.\\n    Quote: In its most recent fiscal quarter (ended in late April), revenue hit a record $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% from the prior quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e313, e399; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e361 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Broadcom and Broadcom management ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Broadcom reported AI chip revenue of $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% year over year, and management expected roughly $16 billion this quarter.\\n    Quote: Its AI chip revenue jumped 143% year over year last quarter to $10.8 billion, and management sees roughly $16 billion this quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e194, e402; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e364 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] The author says NVIDIA\\u2019s forward earnings multiple recently fell to roughly 18x, its lowest since before the AI boom and more than 50% below its five-year average.\\n    Quote: Although Nvidia still trades at a premium to most semiconductor companies, its earnings multiple recently fell to its lowest level since before the AI boom at roughly 18 times forward earnings. That's a more than 50% discount from its own five-year average.\\n- e365 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] The author estimates NVIDIA\\u2019s current forward P/E ratio at about 23x.\\n    Quote: Currently, Nvidia has a forward price-to-earnings (P/E) ratio closer to 23 times.\\n- e366 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] The author estimates NVIDIA\\u2019s price-to-sales ratio at about 22x and says it reflects expectations of continued rapid growth.\\n    Quote: However, its price-to-sales (P/S) ratio remains elevated at around 22 times, showing expectations for continued rapid growth.\\n- e367 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] The author reports NVIDIA\\u2019s PEG ratio near 0.45x and says analysts\\u2019 expected earnings growth more than justifies the valuation.\\n    Quote: Still, the P/E-to-growth (PEG) ratio sits near 0.45 times, suggesting analysts still expect earnings growth to more than justify today's valuation.\\n- e368 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst), reporting a Bloomberg survey; original source Bloomberg survey of Chinese technology companies ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] A Bloomberg survey found Chinese technology companies expect domestic suppliers to receive roughly 46% of their AI-chip spending over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: A new Bloomberg survey showed Chinese technology companies expect to allocate roughly 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e235; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e369 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] The author estimates NVIDIA has roughly 85% of the global AI GPU market.\\n    Quote: Nvidia still controls roughly 85% of the global AI GPU market\\n- e370 [fact; barchart.com (analyst), reporting NVIDIA\\u2019s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in FY2027 Q1, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e349, e407, e412, e459; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e371 [fact; barchart.com (analyst), reporting NVIDIA\\u2019s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 net income of $58.3 billion, more than triple the year-earlier amount, and GAAP EPS of $2.39.\\n    Quote: Net income more than tripled to $58.3 billion, while GAAP EPS reached $2.39.\\n- e372 [fact; barchart.com (analyst), reporting NVIDIA\\u2019s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA generated $48.6 billion of free cash flow in FY2027 Q1 and returned roughly $20 billion to shareholders through buybacks and dividends.\\n    Quote: Free cash flow totaled an enormous $48.6 billion, allowing Nvidia to return roughly $20 billion to shareholders through buybacks and dividends.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e132; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e373 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst), reporting NVIDIA management guidance; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided to approximately $91 billion in total revenue for FY2027 Q2, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e351; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e374 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e187 (); both are in force: Nvidia announced plans to launch its Vera Rubin Space-1 Module at an unspecified future date.\\n- e375 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA expanded partnerships with Alphabet and Marvell.\\n    Quote: expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL)\\n- e376 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\\n    Quote: further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\\n- e377 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst), reporting Morgan Stanley\\u2019s view; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Morgan Stanley maintained its Overweight rating and $288 NVIDIA price target, citing the company\\u2019s market position and relative value among AI-processor companies.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley recently maintained an \\\"Overweight\\\" rating and a $288 price target, arguing Nvidia remains the best value among AI processor companies because of its dominant market position.\\n- e378 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst), reporting Goldman Sachs\\u2019s view; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Goldman Sachs reiterated its Buy rating and $250 NVIDIA price target in May, saying management continues to demonstrate healthy enterprise AI spending.\\n    Quote: In May, Goldman Sachs also reiterated its \\\"Buy\\\" rating on NVDA stock with a $250 target, saying management continues to demonstrate that enterprise AI spending remains healthy.\\n- e379 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst), reporting Bank of America\\u2019s view; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Bank of America raised its NVIDIA price target to $350, citing the Vera CPU platform as one of the company\\u2019s most important product launches in years.\\n    Quote: Bank of America is even more optimistic, raising its price target to $350, citing Nvidia's new Vera CPU platform as one of the company's most important product launches in years.\\n- e380 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] The article reports that, among 49 analysts covering NVIDIA, 43 rated it Strong Buy, three Moderate Buy, two Hold and one Strong Sell; the average price target was $302.55, implying 43% upside.\\n    Quote: Of the 49 analysts covering Nvidia, 43 rate the stock as a \\\"Strong Buy,\\\" three have a \\\"Moderate Buy\\\" rating, two have a \\\"Hold,\\\" and one analyst has a \\\"Strong Sell.\\\" The average price target sits at $302.55, suggesting 43% potential upside from here.\\n- e383 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] NVIDIA automotive head Xinzhou Wu said automotive computing needs are growing roughly tenfold every two years.\\n    Quote: Roughly we are talking about 10 times every two years.\\n- e384 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said NVIDIA chip prices would most likely need to rise because demand for chips is intense.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\\n- e385 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said NVIDIA continues to invest in autonomous-vehicle technology by allocating internal compute and fabrication capacity.\\n    Quote: We keep investing in this technology and in this future, not only by allocating internal compute, but with fab capacity as well.\\n- e386 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Tesla CEO Elon Musk is probably ahead of competitors in basic L2++ driver-assistance technology.\\n    Quote: For the basic L2++ technology, Elon is probably ahead of everybody.\\n- e387 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said NVIDIA plans to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners\\u2019 vehicles across the United States by the end of 2026.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States.\\n- e388 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said NVIDIA and partners including Uber are working toward rolling out an L4 service in the next few years, a plan announced at GTC.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\\n- e389 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers are in NVIDIA\\u2019s Hyperion ecosystem for Level 4 autonomy.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia\\u2019s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\\n- e390 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu estimated that cars are driven 13 trillion miles annually and autonomous driving accounts for about 0.006% of those miles.\\n    Quote: If you look at it, among all the cars, we drive 13 trillion miles per year. Right now the percentage of autonomous miles among all the mileage driven is probably negligible. I think it\\u2019s 0.006%, or something like that.\\n- e391 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Citi ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Citi said NVIDIA has strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical AI-system component.\\n    Quote: The bank pointed to Nvidia's strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\\n- e393 [party_statement; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to account for a larger share of future growth.\\n    Quote: It expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to make up a larger share of future growth as AI adoption expands.\\n- e398 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f4eb5206f2995f5dbb86c5e9 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported quarterly revenue of $81.6 billion for the quarter ended April 26, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In its most recent quarter (ended April 26), it made $81.6 billion in revenue (up 85% year over year)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e264, e417; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e399 [fact; fool.com (Danny Vena); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal 2027 first quarter (ended April 26), Nvidia generated record revenue, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter to $81.6 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e359; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e401 [party_statement; fool.com (Danny Vena); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA management forecast Q2 total revenue of $91 billion, up 95% year over year.\\n    Quote: Management expects its growth spurt to continue, forecasting year-over-year revenue growth of 95% to $91 billion in Q2.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e316, e470; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e402 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing Broadcom\\u2019s reported results; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom reported Q2 FY2026 revenue of $22.187 billion, up 47.9%, and AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion, up 143%.\\n    Quote: Broadcom\\u2019s Q2 FY2026 revenue hit $22.187 billion, up 47.9%, with AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion growing 143%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e361, e456; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e403 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, quoting Broadcom CEO Hock Tan; original source Hock Tan, Broadcom CEO ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan attributed the sales mix to increasing demand for custom AI accelerators and AI networking.\\n    Quote: CEO Hock Tan said the mix is being \\u201cdriven by increasing demand for custom AI accelerators and AI networking.\\u201d\\n- e404 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, reporting Broadcom management\\u2019s guidance; original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom management guided to $16.0 billion of AI revenue, about 54% of total sales, for Q3 FY2026.\\n    Quote: Broadcom\\u2019s Q3 earnings report lands September 8, and management has already telegraphed $16.0 billion in AI revenue, roughly 54% of total sales.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e195; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e405 [fact; 247wallst.com, citing NVIDIA\\u2019s reported results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, and Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion; networking revenue was up 199%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s Q1 FY2027 revenue reached $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, with Data Center at $75.246 billion and networking alone up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e155, e469, e476, e578; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e406 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, describing NVIDIA\\u2019s guidance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA\\u2019s Q2 guidance assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA leans on scale and CUDA gravity, but assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue in Q2 guidance, a headwind Broadcom does not carry to the same degree.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e317; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e407 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:301b0738dab6ca32e88b019a 2026-07-13] NVIDIA