f $5.775 billion.\\n- e416 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, reporting Broadcom\\u2019s figure and its CEO\\u2019s target; original source Broadcom; CEO Hock Tan for the target ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] Broadcom reported Q2 FY2026 AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion, up 143% year over year; CEO Hock Tan targeted $100 billion in AI sales by 2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY26 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, up 143% YoY, and CEO Hock Tan is targeting $100 billion in AI sales by 2027.\\n- e417 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, for its spring quarter.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA ( NASDAQ: NVDA ) followed with $81.615 billion and 85.23% growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e398; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e419 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA shipped zero H20 chips to China in its spring quarter, compared with $4.6 billion of H20 shipments a year earlier.\\n    Quote: Yet zero H20 chips shipped to China this quarter, versus $4.6 billion a year ago.\\n- e421 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source Meta Platforms ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta launched Meta Compute, a service that rents its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Quote: then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e225 (2026-07-01); both are in force: Bloomberg reported that Meta was setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models, reported July 1, 2026.\\n- e422 [party_statement; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, for Q2, excluding China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided to $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, explicitly excluding China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e351; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e430 [third_party_view; Justin Pope; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Goldman Sachs estimates AI compute spending at approximately $494 billion in calendar 2026, rising to $1.13 trillion by 2031.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates that AI compute spending will grow from approximately $494 billion this year to $1.13 trillion by 2031.\\n- e431 [party_statement; Justin Pope; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said he sees at least $1 trillion in revenue from Blackwell and Rubin through the end of calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, CEO Jensen Huang has said that he sees at least $1 trillion in revenue from Nvidia's Blackwell and Rubin platforms through the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e35; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e433 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source TSMC ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] TSMC raised its forecast for global semiconductor revenue by 2030 from $1 trillion, citing AI-fueled chip demand.\\n    Quote: The Taiwan-based foundry giant had previously anticipated $1 trillion in semiconductor revenue by the end of the decade. However, AI-fueled demand for chips led to a substantial upgrade to its guidance.\\n- e434 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source TSMC ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] TSMC estimates AI and HPC chips will make up 55% of the global semiconductor market opportunity it forecasts for 2030.\\n    Quote: TSMC points out that AI and high-performance computing (HPC) chips will account for 55% of this lucrative opportunity.\\n- e435 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source fool.com analyst 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] The author calculates that TSMC's forecast implies an $825 billion addressable market for Nvidia in AI data center chips.\\n    Quote: That puts Nvidia's addressable opportunity in the AI data center chip market at an impressive $825 billion.\\n- e438 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source fool.com analyst 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] The author estimates NVIDIA has an 80% share of the AI accelerator market.\\n    Quote: with an estimated 80% share.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e464; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e439 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source fool.com analyst 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] The author says NVIDIA's AI chip market share is expected to fall to 75% in 2026.\\n    Quote: That's why Nvidia's AI chip market share is anticipated to decline to 75% this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e340; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e440 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source fool.com analyst 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] In a scenario where NVIDIA's AI-chip market share falls to 50% in 2030, the author calculates it could still generate more than $400 billion in Data Center chip revenue that year, based on an $825 billion market.\\n    Quote: Let's assume Nvidia continues to lose ground in AI chips for the next four years and ends up at just 50% market share in 2030; it can still generate more than $400 billion in data center chip revenue in 2030 (based on the $825 billion market size estimated above).\\n- e443 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source Mordor Intelligence ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Mordor Intelligence forecasts annual growth of 36% for the InfiniBand market over the next five years.\\n    Quote: The InfiniBand market, for instance, is expected to clock 36% annual growth over the next five years, according to Mordor Intelligence.\\n- e444 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source Mordor Intelligence ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Mordor Intelligence estimates the InfiniBand market could generate more than $164 billion in revenue in 2031.\\n    Quote: It could generate more than $164 billion in revenue in 2031.\\n- e445 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source Dell'Oro Group ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Dell'Oro Group projects the data center switch market will exceed $100 billion in revenue by 2030.\\n    Quote: the data center switch market is projected to exceed $100 billion in revenue by 2030, according to Dell'Oro Group.\\n- e446 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source fool.com analyst 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] The author estimates NVIDIA's combined Data Center compute and networking addressable opportunity could exceed $1 trillion by 2030.\\n    Quote: In all, Nvidia's data center addressable opportunity, including both networking and compute, could surpass $1 trillion by the end of the decade.\\n- e447 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source analysts ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Analysts forecast NVIDIA FY2027 earnings per share of $8.97, an 88% increase.\\n    Quote: Analysts are projecting an 88% spike in Nvidia's earnings in fiscal 2027 (ending in January 2027) to $8.97 per share.\\n- e459 [fact; 247wallst.com, reporting the figure; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: It delivered $81.615 billion in Q1 FY27 revenue, up 85.23% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e370, e474; the argum