stom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers in the long run, leading to potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion.\\n- e467 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting Financial Times reporting based on sources; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reportedly cut its authorized-client roster in Asia by more than half after tougher compliance inspections, including customer-site visits, contract checks, and end-user interviews, to reduce chip smuggling into China.\\n    Quote: According to the Financial Times , this roster cuts the number of authorized clients by more than half, with those remaining having passed tougher compliance inspections to ensure that they are genuine businesses, not shell companies designed to forward Nvidia GPUs and servers into China. Some of the steps that Nvidia took to help safeguard its chips reportedly included sending staff to customer d\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e565; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e468 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.6 billion, up 85.2% YoY,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e412; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e469 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027, driven by InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\\n    Quote: with Data Center Networking alone growing 199% on InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e405; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e470 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54