r\\u2019s view; original source Morningstar 2026-07-30; from gnews:8793fc7a18c40c2f4f76ad10 2026-07-31] Morningstar forecast NVIDIA revenue growth of 80% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Morningstar sees Nvidia posting 80% revenue growth in 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e891; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e1519 [party_statement; Zacks; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:6f53d290d7aa54066ad3f160 2026-07-31] NVIDIA management guided FY2027 Q2 total revenue to $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\\n    Quote: Management further expects AI demand to remain robust, as they project NVIDIA\\u2019s fiscal second-quarter 2027 revenues to come in at $91 billion, plus or minus 2%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e985; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e1604 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Elon Musk, SpaceX CEO 2026-08-05; from gnews:baaf41a9a32da4e5efcfd131 2026-08-05] SpaceX CEO Elon Musk said SpaceX will build its AI services exclusively on NVIDIA systems going forward.\\n    Quote: \\\"So we're exclusive to Nvidia.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1590, e1608, e1615; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e1605 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Elon Musk, SpaceX CEO 2026-08-05; from gnews:baaf41a9a32da4e5efcfd131 2026-08-05] Elon Musk said SpaceX expects computing capacity to exceed 2 GW by year-end 2026 and reach close to 10 GW by year-end 2027.\\n    Quote: According to the CEO, SpaceX expects to end the year with more than 2 gigawatts of compute and anticipates having close to 10 gigawatts of computing capacity by the end of next year.\\n- e1606 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Elon Musk, SpaceX CEO 2026-08-05; from gnews:baaf41a9a32da4e5efcfd131 2026-08-05] Elon Musk said SpaceX plans to launch NVIDIA's Vera Rubin NVL72 rackscale system on the ground and in space as part of its Starmind satellite program.\\n    Quote: Musk also said that the company plans to launch Nvidia's Vera Rubin NVL72 rackscale system both on the ground and in space as part of its Starmind satellite program.\\n- e1613 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Lisa Su, AMD CEO 2026-08-04; from gnews:7ce0b7c3361fc5060098941f 2026-08-05] AMD CEO Lisa Su said AMD expects server revenue to grow 80% year over year in the second half of 2026 and more than 70% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Su told analysts on the earnings call Tuesday that the company expects server revenue to grow 80% year-over-year in the second half of 2026 and more than 70% for 2027.\\n- e1637 [party_statement; Nokia; original source Indosat Ooredoo Hutchison 2026-08-06; from gnews:211ef1e93536bca4527f679e 2026-08-06] Indosat said Zankore plans to deliver approximately 200 MW of AI capacity in the first half of 2027, powered by NVIDIA GB300 NVL72.\\n    Quote: Zankore will deliver approximately 200 megawatts (MW) of AI capacity in the first half of 2027, powered by NVIDIA GB300 NVL72.\\n- e1639 [fact; Fortune, reporting; original source Ooredoo Group ; from gnews:5da1731c30b6d1c3a1602cb3 2026-08-06] Zankore has secured customers for about 200 MW of AI capacity planned for the first half of 2027.\\n    Quote: It has already secured blue-chip customers for around 200 MW of AI capacity planned for the first half of 2027.\\n- e1682 [third_party_view; Alex Sirois; original source Alex Sirois 2026-08-08; from gnews:1e5ae2752ae901af3268b2a3 2026-08-08] The author says Broadcom is building custom silicon intended to reduce hyperscalers\\u2019 dependence on NVIDIA\\u2019s platform.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA ( NASDAQ:NVDA | NVDA Price Prediction ) and Broadcom ( NASDAQ:AVGO ) just closed earnings seasons that framed the AI chip war clearly. NVIDIA sells the standardized picks and shovels every hyperscaler needs. Broadcom builds the custom silicon those same hyperscalers hope will reduce their dependence on Jensen Huang\\u2019s platform.\\n- e1683 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e5ae2752ae901af3268b2a3 2026-08-08] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year, including $75.246 billion of Data Center revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s Q1 FY2027 delivered $81.615 billion in revenue, up 85.23% year over year, with Data Center alone hitting $75.246 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e467; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e1684 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e5ae2752ae901af3268b2a3 2026-08-08] NVIDIA Data Center networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Networking inside that segment climbed 199%, a number that matters more than the Blackwell 300 headlines.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e465; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e1685 [party_statement; Alex Sirois; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:1e5ae2752ae901af3268b2a3 2026-08-08] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: Huang framed it plainly: \\u201cThe buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\u201d\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e966; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e1686 [party_statement; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e5ae2752ae901af3268b2a3 2026-08-08] NVIDIA guided Q2 revenue to $91.0 billion excluding China.\\n    Quote: Guidance for Q2 landed at $91.0 billion, excluding China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e680; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e1687 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:1e5ae2752ae901af3268b2a3 2026-08-08] Broadcom report