able for its RX 7000-series GPUs earlier in 2026.\\n    Quote: AMD opened up FSR 4 Upscaling 4.1 for the RX 7000 series earlier this year, proving that it was possible.\\n- e1913 [fact; Monica J. White, How-To Geek; original source AMD ; from gnews:1bfc54808924d17144ab4961 2026-08-12] AMD recently enabled Advanced Shader Delivery across all RDNA generations, including RX 5000- and RX 6000-series cards.\\n    Quote: AMD enabled it recently, across every RDNA generation, and that includes even the old(ish) RX 5000 and RX 6000 cards.\\n- e1914 [third_party_view; Monica J. White, How-To Geek; original source Monica J. White, How-To Geek 2026-08-12; from gnews:1bfc54808924d17144ab4961 2026-08-12] The author reported that NVIDIA did not yet support Advanced Shader Delivery as of 2026-08-12.\\n    Quote: Now, the best part is that Nvidia doesn't support this yet.\\n- e1920 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source CoreWeave 2026-08-10; from gnews:011203b517e045ffe773b1fb 2026-08-12] CoreWeave signed a contract for Nvidia A100 GPUs extending into 2029.\\n    Quote: CoreWeave signed a contract for Nvidia A100 GPUs that runs into 2029, nine years after the Ampere-based SKU debuted, CEO Mike Intrator disclosed on the company's second-quarter earnings call on Monday.\\n- e1921 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source CoreWeave ; from gnews:011203b517e045ffe773b1fb 2026-08-12] CoreWeave reported quarterly revenue of $2.58 billion, up 112% year over year, and a $104 billion revenue backlog excluding more than $25 billion in new commitments booked since July.\\n    Quote: The company reported $2.58 billion in quarterly revenue, up 112% year over year, and a $104 billion revenue backlog that excludes more than $25 billion in new commitments booked since July.\\n- e1922 [party_statement; Tom's Hardware; original source CoreWeave CEO Mike Intrator 2026-08-10; from gnews:011203b517e045ffe773b1fb 2026-08-12] CoreWeave CEO Mike Intrator said prices for prior-generation GPU SKUs were at or above their levels from years earlier.\\n    Quote: In remarks made during the earnings call, Intrator said, \\u201cpricing for prior generation SKUs is at or above where it was years ago.\\u201d\\n- e1923 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source CoreWeave 2026-08-10; from gnews:011203b517e045ffe773b1fb 2026-08-12] CoreWeave's contracted power was 3.7 GW in Q2 and 4.2 GW as of 2026-08-10, compared with 1.5 GW online.\\n    Quote: CoreWeave's contracted power grew to 3.7 GW in Q2 and stood at 4.2 GW as of Monday, against just 1.5 GW online, so customer commitments already cover nearly triple the capacity the company can deliver.\\n- e1924 [party_statement; Tom's Hardware; original source CoreWeave CFO Nitin Agrawal 2026-08-10; from gnews:011203b517e045ffe773b1fb 2026-08-12] CoreWeave CFO Nitin Agrawal said capacity due for renewal represented a very limited share of its fleet and older-generation GPU average selling prices were at or above year-earlier levels.\\n    Quote: CFO Nitin Agrawal added on the call that capacity coming up for renewal represents a very limited share of CoreWeave's fleet, with older-generation ASPs at or above levels from a year ago.\\n\\n[Themes in force, 8]\\n- v10 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Chinese authorities formally authorize purchases of Nvidia H200 chips by Chinese AI companies by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-08-12; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus or stated deadline is supplied, so the status-quo reference is no formal Chinese authorization by January 31, 2027. The strongest evidence now goes beyond a prospective pathway: e1886 reports that China granted approvals for H200 purchases by ByteDan\\n- v18 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will the Remote Access Security Act be enacted by December 31, 2026?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-07-29; reasons: The reference is the latest supplied legislative status, not a supplied market-consensus estimate: the Act passed the House but was still awaiting Senate action, which places the baseline at rung 2 (No). The evidence implies it is more likely than not to remain unenacted on December 31: with about s\\n- v25 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will Taiwan adopt restrictions on AI chip sales to China by December 31, 2026?: now rung 1 No; judged 2026-07-29; reasons: The reference is Taiwan\\u2019s current policy status: no Taiwan-specific restrictions on AI chip sales to China, which sits at rung 1. The new, specific report that Taiwan is considering a criminal ban moves the forecast toward adoption, as does the smuggling investigation, but consideration is not an ad\\n- v26 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will Taiwan adopt performance-threshold controls on exports of advanced AI chips by December 31, 2026?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-07-28; reasons: No market consensus or formal target is supplied; the reference is the status-quo baseline of no adopted controls, rung 2. Consultations and active consideration make adoption more plausible than before, but the Ministry confirmed that no timeline is set. With the deadline only five months away, the\\n- v32 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will the Commerce Department announce or adopt restrictions on Chinese AI developers' access to advanced chips through overseas data centers by December 31, 2026?: now rung 1 No; judged 2026-08-07; reasons: No market consensus, official timetable, or proposed rule is supplied; the status-quo reference is rung 1. The active Commerce review is a concrete signal toward restrictions, but the report only says the department is examining access, while the analyst says it could close the loophole eventually. \\n- v6 (ai-capex, due 2027-02-28) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?: now rung 4 Upper-middle range; judged 2026-08-11; reasons: The market reference is about $650 billion for 2026, which sits in rung 3. The current company-level outlook implies roughly $760\\u2013$770 billion: Alphabet at about $200 billion, Amazon at $220 billion, Meta at about $135 billion using the midpoint of its $125\\u2013$145 billion guidance, and Microsoft at th\\n- v7 (ai-capex, due 2028-02-28) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?: now rung 3 Neutral; judged 2026-08-11; reasons: The reference is NVIDIA management\\u2019s forecast that 2027 spending will top $1 trillion, which sits in rung 3; the reported $650 billion 2026 estimate and the stated increase imply substantial growth, not a flat annualization of the last quarter. The implied 2027 outcome remains roughly $1.0\\u2013$1.1 tril\\n- v9 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will Congress enact legislation phasing out Chinese-made lidar technology in the United States by December 31, 2026?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-07-07; reasons: The reference is No (rung 2): no market consensus or enacted legislation is supplied, and the stated deadline remains the test. The House committee\\u2019s proposal is a concrete step toward enactment, but it is not enactment by Congress; with only this evidence, it raises the chance of Yes without making\\n\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 2; reasons: The reference is the $392 billion analyst estimate, which is rung 2. The latest operating path remains consistent with revenue modestly above that estimate, but does not imply the $431.2 billion needed for rung 1. The new $103.1 billion Q3 figure is an analyst expectation, not company guidance; it reinforces the growth sequence without establishing a higher full-year run-rate. Supply, China and competition risks offset some of the demand and investment signals.\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\", \"role\": \"user\"}], \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\", \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\", \"response_format\": {\"json_schema\": {\"name\": \"judgement\", \"schema\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"changed\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"cites\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"cites_views\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"implied_outcome\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"pushes\": {\"items\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"evidence_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"push\": {\"enum\": [\"toward_first\", \"toward_last\", \"none\"], \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"evidence_id\", \"push\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"reasons\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"reference\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"rung\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"theme_pushes\": {\"items\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"push\": {\"enum\": [\"toward_first\", \"toward_last\", \"none\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"view_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"view_id\", \"push\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"why_changed\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"rung\", \"reference\", \"implied_outcome\", \"reasons\", \"cites\", \"cites_views\", \"pushes\", \"changed\", \"why_changed\", \"theme_pushes\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"strict\": true}, \"type\": \"json_schema\"}}]\n[\"old-3\", 4101, {\"max_completion_tokens\": 16000, \"messages\": [{\"content\": \"You are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\\n\\n- Rejudge from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently), the current conclusions of dependencies and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\\n- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\\n- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \\\"not established\\\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\\n- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\\n- \\u201cThemes in force\\u201d lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \\u201cupdated since this thesis was last judged\\u201d may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\\n- A dependency marked \\u201cnot yet created\\u201d supplies no input. A dependency marked \\u201chistorical only\\u201d is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\\n- Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\\n- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_fi\n... 686781 bytes omitted ...\nwasaki Heavy Industries, intend to join, according to Nvidia.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e500, e568; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e470 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source International Trade Administration ; from gnews:e0d639dfc05f3b1a61af4c75 2026-07-16] The International Trade Administration expects Japan's AI market to reach $27.9 billion by 2029.\\n    Quote: Japan's AI market is expected to reach $27.9 billion by 2029, opening doors for U.S. firms to invest, according to the International Trade Administration.\\n- e471 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e0d639dfc05f3b1a61af4c75 2026-07-16] NVIDIA highlighted the ongoing expansion of Tokyo-1, the AI drug-discovery consortium operated by Xeureka, a Mitsui subsidiary.\\n    Quote: When it comes to agentic AI, Nvidia highlighted the ongoing expansion of Tokyo-1, the AI drug discovery consortium operated by Xeureka, a Mitsui subsidiary.\\n- e482 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source Keithen Drury 2026-07-16; from gnews:e4e37eb5cc64ccfb65317770 2026-07-16] Keithen Drury cited expected NVIDIA growth of 41% next year; the item does not specify the measure.\\n    Quote: With 41% growth expected next year, that leaves a lot of room for upside during the next year.\\n- e486 [fact; Automotive World, reporting; original source Toyota and NVIDIA 2026-07-16; from gnews:a266d683ea788b6b1a5a9806 2026-07-16] Toyota will integrate NVIDIA\\u2019s Omniverse, Isaac robotics platform and Nemotron models across Woven City prototype development and vehicle assembly lines under an expanded partnership announced July 16, 2026.\\n    Quote: The expanded deal, announced 16 July, will see Toyota integrate Nvidia\\u2019s Omniverse, Isaac robotics platform and Nemotron large language models across its Woven City prototype development and vehicle assembly lines.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e448; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e487 [fact; Automotive World, reporting; original source Fujitsu, Fanuc, Kawasaki Heavy Industries, Yaskawa Electric, Hitachi, NEC, Komatsu and Kubota ; from gnews:a266d683ea788b6b1a5a9806 2026-07-16] Fujitsu, Fanuc, Kawasaki Heavy Industries, Yaskawa Electric, Hitachi, NEC, Komatsu and Kubota joined NVIDIA\\u2019s Cosmos Coalition during the week of July 16, 2026, to accelerate adoption of NVIDIA platforms in robotics, factory automation, self-driving vehicles and smart infrastructure.\\n    Quote: with Fujitsu, Fanuc, Kawasaki Heavy Industries, Yaskawa Electric, Hitachi, NEC, Komatsu and Kubota all joining its Cosmos Coalition in the same week. They are collectively working to accelerate adoption of Nvidia\\u2019s platforms across humanoid robots, factory automation, self-driving vehicles, and smart infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e535; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e488 [party_statement; Automotive World, reporting; original source Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi\\u2019s government ; from gnews:a266d683ea788b6b1a5a9806 2026-07-16] The Japanese government set a target for Japanese companies to capture 30% of the global AI robotics market and a JP\\u00a520 trillion (US$123 billion) share of the industry by 2040.\\n    Quote: Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi\\u2019s government has set an aggressive target for Japanese companies to capture 30% of the global AI robotics market and secure a JP\\u00a520tr (US$123bn) share of the industry by 2040\\n- e492 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a2bb93d437d80c346c1d80a4 2026-07-16] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61 billion , up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion (+92% YoY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e204; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e493 [third_party_view; Vandita Jadeja; original source Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-16; from gnews:a2bb93d437d80c346c1d80a4 2026-07-16] The author says NVIDIA EPS would compound if Blackwell 300 and Vera Rubin meet ramps at Meta, CoreWeave, and Anthropic, supporting the $400 target\\u2019s valuation case.\\n    Quote: If Blackwell 300 and Vera Rubin deliver on Meta\\u2019s, CoreWeave\\u2019s, and Anthropic\\u2019s ramps, EPS compounds, and the 50x multiple becomes the compression story rather than an expansion stretch.\\n- e494 [third_party_view; Vandita Jadeja; original source Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-16; from gnews:a2bb93d437d80c346c1d80a4 2026-07-16] The author says NVIDIA\\u2019s guidance assumes zero China Data Center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: The risk: China Data Center revenue remains zero in guidance due to export restrictions .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e350; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e496 [party_statement; es.tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:62714f928bfeae1c78139609 2026-07-16] NVIDIA reported that sovereign AI revenue exceeded $30 billion in FY2026, more than tripling year over year.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said revenue from sovereign AI\\u2014government-backed efforts to develop independent artificial intelligence capabilities\\u2014more than tripled year over year to more than $30 billion in fiscal 2026.\\n- e497 [party_statement; es.tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:62714f928bfeae1c78139609 2026-07-16] NVIDIA said it expects sovereign AI revenue to grow further; no period or amount was specified.\\n    Quote: The company said it expects further growth from the segment.\\n- e498 [fact; es.tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:62714f928bfeae1c78139609 2026-07-16] NVIDIA introduced the T3000 and T2000 supercomputing modules, based on its Thor architecture.\\n    Quote: The company introduced two new supercomputing modules, the T3000 and T2000, based on its Thor computing architecture.\\n- e499 [fact; es.tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-15; from gnews:62714f928bfeae1c78139609 2026-07-16] NVIDIA unveiled Cosmos 3 Edge, an AI model for robots and vision AI agents, on 2026-07-15.\\n    Quote: On Wednesday, Nvidia also unveiled Cosmos 3 Edge, a new artificial intelligence model for robots and vision AI agents.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e468; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e500 [party_statement; es.tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:62714f928bfeae1c78139609 2026-07-16] Fujitsu, Hitachi, and Kawasaki Heavy Industries intend to join a coalition to advance physical AI technologies in Japan, according to NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: According to the company, Fujitsu, Hitachi, and Kawasaki Heavy Industries intend to join a coalition aimed at advancing physical AI technologies in Japan.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e469; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e506 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:19d750b9d8c73eecff5a0018 2026-07-16] NVIDIA revenue was $81.615 billion in the most recent quarter, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: revenue grew 85.23% year over year to $81.615 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e287; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e507 [party_statement; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:19d750b9d8c73eecff5a0018 2026-07-16] NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91.0 billion for Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91.0 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e349, e540; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e516 [party_statement; Kyodo News; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO 2026-07-16; from gnews:8fa80c5fdfe362f5c1cc1452 2026-07-16] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said on July 16, 2026, that NVIDIA would help Japan develop a domestic AI foundation model by providing advanced AI chips.\\n    Quote: Nvidia Corp. CEO Jensen Huang said Thursday his company will help Japan develop a domestic artificial intelligence foundation model by providing advanced AI chips as part of its deeper ties with the country's technology industry.\\n- e527 [third_party_view; ifre.com; original source ifre.com 2026-07-16; from gnews:dc1bf55ec327aa54f2561647 2026-07-16] Rental rates for older-generation NVIDIA H100 cards have rebounded in 2026 from their 2024\\u20132025 lows.\\n    Quote: While bankers also noted that GPUs have been considered as short-lived and weak collateral, there is room for optimism as rental rates for older\\u2011generation Nvidia H100 cards have rebounded this year from the lows of 2024\\u20132025.\\n- e530 [fact; Healthcare IT Today; original source Verkada 2026-07-01; from gnews:e71c7f52a1d727e1387644cd 2026-07-16] Verkada announced a collaboration with NVIDIA to develop and deploy physical AI across the built environment.\\n    Quote: Verkada , a leader in AI-powered physical security and operations, today announced a collaboration with NVIDIA to accelerate the development and deployment of physical AI across the built environment.\\n- e531 [party_statement; AFP; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:2e9d5650d9e525482062cc00 2026-07-16] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI technology cycle was at its beginning and that technology cycles typically last 10 to 15 years before plateauing.\\n    Quote: \\\"Most technology cycles last anywhere from 10 to 15 years before it kind of plateaus. We are at the beginning of this one,\\\" the US chip giant's CEO told reporters in Tokyo.\\n- e532 [party_statement; AFP; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:2e9d5650d9e525482062cc00 2026-07-16] Jensen Huang said AI demand would never decline, comparing it with electricity.\\n    Quote: \\\"Is it going to flatten out? It will never go down, just as electricity never went down,\\\" he said, adding that semiconductors will be the world's largest industry, as part of its \\\"social fabric.\\\"\\n- e533 [fact; AFP; original source Kawasaki Heavy Industries ; from gnews:2e9d5650d9e525482062cc00 2026-07-16] NVIDIA and Kawasaki Heavy Industries announced they will co-develop AI-powered robots for shipbuilding.\\n    Quote: Nvidia and Kawasaki Heavy Industries will co-develop AI-powered robots for use in shipbuilding, the Japanese firm said Thursday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e536; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e535 [fact; AFP; original source NVIDIA and Fujitsu ; from gnews:2e9d5650d9e525482062cc00 2026-07-16] NVIDIA announced a robotics collaboration with Fujitsu and other parties.\\n    Quote: Other tie-ups announced included a collaboration on robotics with Japan's Fujitsu and others.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e487; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e536 [fact; The Standard; original source Kawasaki Heavy Industries 2026-07-16; from gnews:2f4507655e71fa84c802639f 2026-07-16] NVIDIA and Kawasaki Heavy Industries announced plans to co-develop AI-powered shipbuilding robots on 2026-07-16.\\n    Quote: Nvidia and Kawasaki Heavy Industries will co-develop AI-powered robots for use in shipbuilding, the Japanese firm said Thursday during a visit to Tokyo by the US chip giant's CEO Jensen Huang.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e533; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e539 [fact; 247Wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:3cfa18ac4b56d1885013308d 2026-07-16] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY2027, reported on May 20, 2026, delivered: revenue of $81.615 billion grew 85.23% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e345; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e540 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA management 2026-05-20; from gnews:3cfa18ac4b56d1885013308d 2026-07-16] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91.0 billion.\\n    Quote: management guided Q2 to $91.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e507; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e548 [fact; 247Wallst author Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2b5982d17c88b8e7433e1e15 2026-07-16] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q1 fiscal 2027 revenue landed at $81.615 billion, up 85.2% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e553 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:0e5b33a0b98c921c5e5db08b 2026-07-16] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.6 billion in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA just posted $81.6 billion in Q1 FY27 revenue\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e269, e571; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e554 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:0e5b33a0b98c921c5e5db08b 2026-07-16] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion, excluding China.\\n    Quote: Guidance for Q2 FY27 is $91 billion, and it excludes China entirely.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e240; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e561 [party_statement; arabnews.jp; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-16; from gnews:663af037ff2294d1ed81cd11 2026-07-16] NVIDIA said on July 16, 2026, that it was partnering with Fanuc and Yaskawa Electric to advance robotics and AI development.\\n    Quote: Nvidia \\u200csaid on Thursday it was partnering with Japanese companies including Fanuc and Yaskawa Electric to advance \\u200bthe development of robotics and AI.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e424; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e562 [fact; arabnews.jp; original source ASML 2026-07-15; from gnews:663af037ff2294d1ed81cd11 2026-07-16] ASML raised its sales forecast and pledged a capacity expansion on July 15, 2026.\\n    Quote: Investors are weighing the strength of the AI investment cycle, with chipmaking equipment maker ASML on Wednesday raising its sales forecast and pledging capacity expansion.\\n- e563 [third_party_view; arabnews.jp; original source arabnews.jp ; from gnews:663af037ff2294d1ed81cd11 2026-07-16] TSMC was expected to post a fifth consecutive quarter of record earnings on July 16, 2026, attributed to the AI boom.\\n    Quote: TSMC, the world\\u2019s leading contract chipmaker, is expected to post a fifth consecutive quarter of record earnings on \\u200bThursday due \\u200bto the AI boom.\\n- e568 [fact; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-16; from gnews:bc598c1ba255001385a08723 2026-07-17] NVIDIA announced an expansion of its AI footprint in Japan through new partnerships.\\n    Quote: The company even announced yesterday that it is expanding its AI footprint in Japan with new partnerships.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e469; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e569 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:03f49670bc6aa3ce8c653170 2026-07-17] NVIDIA reported year-over-year revenue growth of 85% in its latest quarter.\\n    Quote: Despite reporting 85% yearly revenue growth in its latest quarter\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e223; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e571 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:03f49670bc6aa3ce8c653170 2026-07-17] NVIDIA generated $81.6 billion in total revenue in FY2027 Q1, ended April 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: the company generated $81.6 billion in revenue in the first quarter of fiscal 2027 (ended April 26).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e553; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e572 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Analysts ; from gnews:03f49670bc6aa3ce8c653170 2026-07-17] Analysts forecast NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue to increase 82%.\\n    Quote: analysts forecast an 82% revenue surge for fiscal 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e195; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e574 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:e33eeae2e6a898bcf6f75ab6 2026-07-17] Analysts expected NVIDIA to deliver nearly 100% growth in Q2 2026; the article does not specify the growth measure.\\n    Quote: That trend is expected to last through at least Q2, with analysts expecting nearly 100% growth from Nvidia during Q2.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e224; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e577 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c03377d9fbbf30b7a0933cd5 2026-07-17] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue of close to $215.9 billion, up 65.5% year over year.\\n    Quote: In FY 2026, revenue reached close to $215.9 billion, a significant jump of 65.5% over the previous year.\\n- e578 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c03377d9fbbf30b7a0933cd5 2026-07-17] NVIDIA\\u2019s two largest direct customers accounted for 22% and 14% of total sales in the most recent fiscal year.\\n    Quote: Revenue is highly concentrated, with two direct customers accounting for 22% and 14% of total sales in the most recent fiscal year.\\n- e579 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:99d11db52f240a9bdbff8731 2026-07-17] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.6 billion in fiscal Q1 2027, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: Nvidia, which posted $81.6 billion in total revenue for its fiscal first quarter of 2027, an 85% increase from a year earlier.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e589 [third_party_view; Precedence Research; original source Precedence Research 2026-07-17; from gnews:8104fb6cb8a4bcb37d1fe4b7 2026-07-17] Precedence Research projected the global GPU market at USD 136.06 billion in calendar 2026, with a 32.62% CAGR over 2026\\u20132035.\\n    Quote: The global graphics processing unit (GPU) market was valued at USD 101.54 billion in 2025 and is projected to grow from USD 136.06 billion in 2026 to approximately USD 1,712.56 billion by 2035, registering a CAGR of 32.62% during the forecast period from 2026 to 2035.\\n- e590 [fact; Ece Yildirim, Gizmodo; original source Moonshot 2026-07-16; from gnews:86e5102be4f45f9e4dfcdb9d 2026-07-17] Moonshot debuted its Kimi K3 AI model on Thursday, July 16, 2026; the article says it performed highly across multiple benchmarks compared with costlier frontier American AI models.\\n    Quote: On Thursday, Chinese artificial intelligence startup Moonshot debuted its latest model, Kimi K3, a gigantic soon-to-be open-weight model with 2.8 trillion parameters. The announcement sent waves across the American AI industry, particularly for the model\\u2019s high performance across multiple benchmarks compared to the latest costlier offerings from the frontier American AI companies.\\n\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]\\n- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-17\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA\\u2019s approximately $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast is the market reference and sits at the lower boundary of rung 2.\\n    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): Approximately $19 billion in FY2027\\u2014an analytical estimate just below the company\\u2019s roughly $20 billion target, discounted because the evidence describes offers and customer intent but no quantified shipments or deployments.\\n    Reasons (excerpt): The reference is NVIDIA\\u2019s roughly $20 billion FY2027 sales forecast, which sits at the lower boundary of rung 2. I discount that target slightly: cloud offerings are reported, and a customer plans integration, but there is no disclosed shipment volume, deployment timing, or customer demand figure to validate the target. The favorable demand themes support sales but do not supply the quantified volume needed to move the estimate to $20 billion or more.\\n\\n[Themes in force, 3]\\n- v10 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China's authorities authorize Chinese AI companies to purchase Nvidia H200 chips by 2027-01-31?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-07-17; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: No deadline-specific consensus or company guidance is supplied. The observable status quo\\u2014no established Chinese authorization\\u2014sits at rung 2, but the forecast is for the outcome by 2027-01-31, not the status today. Reports citing the same underlying claim say Chinese officials told named firms they\\n- v5 (ai-capex, due 2027-03-31) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?: now rung 3 $600 billion to below $700 billion; judged 2026-07-17; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The market reference is around $650 billion for calendar-2026 data-center capex, which sits in rung 3. The evidence still implies roughly $650 billion for the specific data-center measure: the roughly $800 billion estimate is for broader AI infrastructure, and the $725 billion pledge has no stated s\\n- v6 (ai-capex, due 2028-03-31) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?: now rung 3 $900 billion to below $1.1 trillion; judged 2026-07-16; reasons: The reference is NVIDIA management\\u2019s forecast of more than $1 trillion in 2027, after projected 2026 spending of $650 billion; that reference sits in rung 3. The evidence supports spending above $1 trillion, but does not imply the $1.1 trillion needed to enter rung 4. The qualitative power constrain\\n\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 2; reasons: The reference is Bloomberg's $393 billion FY2027 projection, which sits in rung 3. The Q1 result and Q2 guidance imply about $387 billion for the year if Q2's sequential growth carries through Q3 and Q4; adding the dependency's approximately $19.5 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU forecast, treated as incremental to that run-rate, gives about $407 billion and crosses the $400 billion boundary into rung 2. Booked supply commitments and the updated AI-capex view support the upside, while memory-supply risk and custom-chip alternatives temper confidence; neither supplies a quantified adjustment that takes the implied estimate below $400 billion.\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\", \"role\": \"user\"}], \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\", \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\", \"response_format\": {\"json_schema\": {\"name\": \"judgement\", \"schema\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"changed\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"cites\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"cites_views\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"implied_outcome\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"pushes\": {\"items\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"evidence_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"push\": {\"enum\": [\"toward_first\", \"toward_last\", \"none\"], \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"evidence_id\", \"push\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"reasons\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"reference\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"rung\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"theme_pushes\": {\"items\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"push\": {\"enum\": [\"toward_first\", \"toward_last\", \"none\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"view_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"view_id\", \"push\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"why_changed\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"rung\", \"reference\", \"implied_outcome\", \"reasons\", \"cites\", \"cites_views\", \"pushes\", \"changed\", \"why_changed\", \"theme_pushes\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"strict\": true}, \"type\": \"json_schema\"}}]\n[\"linked-1\", 8766, {\"max_completion_tokens\": 16000, \"messages\": [{\"content\": \"You are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\\n\\n- Rejudge from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently), the current conclusions of dependencies and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\\n- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\\n- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \\\"not established\\\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\\n- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\\n- \\u201cThemes in force\\u201d lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \\u201cupdated since this thesis was last judged\\u201d may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\\n- A dependency marked \\u201cnot yet created\\u201d supplies no input. A dependency marked \\u201chistorical only\\u201d is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\\n- Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\\n- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\\n- changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\\n\", \"role\": \"system\"}, {\"content\": \"Thesis v14 (NVDA, asset, focus \\\"NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue\\\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: Total revenue is at least $450 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: Total revenue is at least $400 billion but less than $450 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: Total revenue is at least $350 billion but less than $400 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: Total revenue is at least $300 billion but less than $350 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: Total revenue is less than $300 billion.\\n\\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 131 items]\\n[Not shown: 33 more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]\\n- e195 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing data compiled by Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg data project NVIDIA FY2027 sales of $393 billion, up 82%, and profits of $228 billion, up 90%.\\n    Quote: The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e572; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e213 [third_party_view; es.tradingview.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:1bfc0e875ab1f26dcf48fb06 2026-07-11] Morgan Stanley said AI laboratories account for roughly 20% of NVIDIA\\u2019s demand; it gave no period.\\n    Quote: The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia\\u2019s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\\n- e219 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts said NVIDIA could lose AI-chip market share in percentage terms while increasing chip sales as the market expands.\\n    Quote: Nvidia can lose share in percentage terms while selling more chips than ever.\\n- e220 [fact; qz.com; original source OpenAI and Broadcom ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] OpenAI\\u2019s announced partnership with Broadcom involves co-developing custom AI chips designed to draw up to 10 gigawatts of power.\\n    Quote: Its partnership with Broadcom $AVGO , announced in October 2025, involves co-developing custom AI chips that will draw up to 10 gigawatts of power, or as much electricity as 10 large nuclear reactors generate.\\n- e221 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that 1.4 million Amazon Trainium chips across three generations were deployed as of March, including more than one million Trainium2 chips running Anthropic\\u2019s Claude.\\n    Quote: As of March, 1.4 million Trainium chips were deployed across three generations, according to TechCrunch , with Anthropic's Claude running on more than one million Trainium2 chips alone.\\n- e222 [fact; qz.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Amazon committed two gigawatts of Trainium computing capacity to OpenAI.\\n    Quote: Amazon has also committed two gigawatts of Trainium computing capacity to OpenAI, putting its chips inside two of the industry's most prominent AI labs.\\n- e229 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source Unnamed supply-chain sources, as reported by tech-insider.org ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] NVIDIA is reportedly cutting RTX 50-series card production by an estimated 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is reportedly cutting production of existing RTX 50-series cards already on shelves by an estimated 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026\\n- e231 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source CNBC (as retold by tech-insider.org) ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron reportedly sold all their 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts, with hyperscalers including Microsoft, Google, Meta, and Amazon buying the supply.\\n    Quote: The root cause sits one layer below Nvidia entirely. Hyperscalers including Microsoft, Google, Meta, and Amazon are buying up high-bandwidth memory as fast as Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron can produce it, and all three manufacturers have reportedly sold out their entire 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts, according to CNBC\\u2019s reporting from January 2026.\\n- e232 [third_party_view; tech-insider.org; original source Micron and Kearney\\u2019s PERLab, as reported by tech-insider.org ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Micron suggested memory supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027 and may return gradually to balance by 2028; Kearney\\u2019s PERLab reportedly projected the shortage could last into 2030.\\n    Quote: Micron has since suggested supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027, with a gradual return to balance by 2028, while other forecasters take a bleaker view: an analysis from Kearney\\u2019s PERLab reportedly projects the shortage could persist into 2030 .\\n- e234 [party_statement; tech-insider.org; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] NVIDIA said AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional NVIDIA GPUs during 2027\\u20132028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said in August 2026 that AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional Nvidia GPUs in 2027 to 2028 .\\n- e238 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e223, e248, e268; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e240 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management forecast approximately $91 billion in fiscal Q2 2027 revenue, assuming no China data-center sales.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e554; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e252 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Chinese technology companies surveyed by Bloomberg ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] A Bloomberg survey reported that Chinese technology companies expect to allocate about 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: A new Bloomberg survey showed Chinese technology companies expect to allocate roughly 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n- e253 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Beijing ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] The author said Beijing had encouraged companies to reduce purchases of foreign AI processors, adding pressure to NVIDIA\\u2019s growth in China.\\n    Quote: Beijing has also encouraged companies to reduce purchases of foreign AI processors, creating additional pressure on Nvidia's long-term growth in one of its largest overseas markets.\\n- e257 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] The author reported that NVIDIA had recently expanded partnerships with Alphabet and Marvell.\\n    Quote: expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL),\\n- e284 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA shipped no H20 compute products to China in Q1 FY2027 and excluded Data Center compute revenue from China from its Q2 FY2027 guidance.\\n    Quote: There were no H20 compute products shipped to China in Q1 FY27, and the Q2 FY27 guidance excludes any Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n- e305 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source TSMC ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] TSMC estimated that AI and HPC chips will account for 55% of the global semiconductor market opportunity it projects for 2030.\\n    Quote: TSMC points out that AI and high-performance computing (HPC) chips will account for 55% of this lucrative opportunity.\\n- e306 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Harsh Chauhan calculated that Nvidia's addressable AI data-center chip market could be $825 billion, based on TSMC's market estimate and AI/HPC share.\\n    Quote: That puts Nvidia's addressable opportunity in the AI data center chip market at an impressive $825 billion.\\n- e309 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source Analysts, as reported by Harsh Chauhan ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Analysts believe NVIDIA's AI data-center chip market share may have peaked.\\n    Quote: However, analysts believe that Nvidia's AI data center chip market share may have peaked.\\n- e310 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source Analysts, as reported by Harsh Chauhan ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Analysts anticipate NVIDIA's AI chip market share will decline to 75% in 2026.\\n    Quote: That's why Nvidia's AI chip market share is anticipated to decline to 75% this year.\\n- e311 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Harsh Chauhan's 2030 scenario assumes NVIDIA has 50% AI-chip market share and estimates more than $400 billion in Data Center chip revenue.\\n    Quote: Let's assume Nvidia continues to lose ground in AI chips for the next four years and ends up at just 50% market share in 2030; it can still generate more than $400 billion in data center chip revenue in 2030 (based on the $825 billion market size estimated above).\\n- e314 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source Mordor Intelligence ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Mordor Intelligence forecast annual InfiniBand market growth of 36% over the next five years.\\n    Quote: The InfiniBand market, for instance, is expected to clock 36% annual growth over the next five years, according to Mordor Intelligence.\\n- e315 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source Mordor Intelligence ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Mordor Intelligence estimated InfiniBand market revenue could exceed $164 billion in 2031.\\n    Quote: It could generate more than $164 billion in revenue in 2031.\\n- e316 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source Dell'Oro Group ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Dell'Oro Group projected data-center switch market revenue would exceed $100 billion by 2030.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, the data center switch market is projected to exceed $100 billion in revenue by 2030, according to Dell'Oro Group.\\n- e317 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Harsh Chauhan estimated NVIDIA's combined Data Center networking and compute addressable opportunity could exceed $1 trillion by 2030.\\n    Quote: In all, Nvidia's data center addressable opportunity, including both networking and compute, could surpass $1 trillion by the end of the decade.\\n- e318 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, Motley Fool; original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Harsh Chauhan reported that consensus revenue-growth projections for NVIDIA through FY2029 had increased significantly.\\n    Quote: That's why there has been a significant jump in Nvidia's consensus revenue growth projections through fiscal 2029.\\n- e321 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:c73b90b63a733c6ab712fcdd 2026-07-14] SK Hynix is slowing its HBM4 ramp and redirecting capacity to conventional DRAM, where shortages have pushed operating margins above HBM margins.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix is deliberately slowing its HBM4 ramp to redirect capacity into conventional DRAM, where shortages have pushed operating margins above HBM's.\\n- e322 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Korean analysts ; from gnews:c73b90b63a733c6ab712fcdd 2026-07-14] Korean analysts estimated that conventional DRAM operating margins were more than 15 percentage points above HBM margins.\\n    Quote: Korean analysts pegged the margin gap at more than 15 points.\\n- e323 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Samsung and SK Hynix ; from gnews:c73b90b63a733c6ab712fcdd 2026-07-14] Samsung reported a 146% increase in DRAM average selling prices in Q1, while SK Hynix's DRAM ASP increase was in the mid-60% range.\\n    Quote: Samsung flagged a 146% DRAM ASP jump in Q1, SK Hynix mid-60%\\n- e324 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source TD Cowen analyst Joshua Buchalter 2026-07-08; from gnews:a0b0f251bbab383483ec679b 2026-07-14] TD Cowen analyst Joshua Buchalter said he remains confident that AI spending will be durable across different applications and customers.\\n    Quote: The analyst remains confident that AI spending is durable throughout different applications and customers.\\n- e329 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: It delivered $81.615 billion in Q1 FY27 revenue, up 85.23% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e272, e345; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e332 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: With quarterly earnings growth of 214.5% YoY and Q2 FY27 revenue guided to $91 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e255, e349; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e337 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, citing the Financial Times; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb 2026-07-14] Nvidia reportedly cut its authorized-client list in Asia by more than half after tougher inspections aimed at preventing GPU and server smuggling into China.\\n    Quote: According to the Financial Times , this roster cuts the number of authorized clients by more than half, with those remaining having passed tougher compliance inspections to ensure that they are genuine businesses, not shell companies designed to forward Nvidia GPUs and servers into China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e376; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e340 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.6 billion, up 85.2% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e343 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided to Q2 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: unusual for a company guiding to $91 billion in Q2 revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e271; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e344 [fact; Phoronix; original source System76 2026-07-14; from gnews:c6024d197f62679f8ff823a3 2026-07-14] System76 announced that its new Adder Pro laptop offers either an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 or RTX 5070 graphics card.\\n    Quote: On the dedicated graphics side is the option for either the GeForce RTX 5060 or RTX 5070 graphics cards.\\n- e345 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue hit $81.615 billion, up 85.23% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e329, e539; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e349 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided to $91 billion in total revenue for Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided Q2 to $91 billion in revenue\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e332, e456, e507; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e350 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 revenue guidance assumes zero Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: which assumes zero China Data Center compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e255, e441, e494; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e351 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61B, up 85.2% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e277, e451; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e355 [fact; rdworldonline.com, reporting; original source Tecan 2026-06-24; from gnews:b46d410f1a3e3ad1888d51de 2026-07-14] Tecan integrated NVIDIA\\u2019s BioNeMo Agent Toolkit into its Introspect cloud analytics platform and opened early access to the agentic AI system for pharmaceutical, biotech and clinical labs on June 24, 2026.\\n    Quote: Tecan\\u2019s latest bet is on agents. The Swiss lab automation company has built agentic AI into Introspect, its cloud analytics platform, using NVIDIA\\u2019s BioNeMo Agent Toolkit, in an announcement on June 24 that opened early access to pharmaceutical, biotech and clinical labs.\\n- e356 [fact; Rest of World; original source Saudi Arabia 2026-06-01; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis running on Nvidia technology.\\n    Quote: Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology \\u2014 from the computer inside each car to the software that steers it.\\n- e369 [fact; blogs.windows.com; original source NVIDIA, Xbox and The Coalition 2026-07-14; from gnews:6ccac7bcb0b813cd4bf29c5d 2026-07-14] NVIDIA, Xbox and The Coalition announced a PC partnership for Gears of War: E-Day, with NVIDIA integrating GeForce RTX technologies and providing performance optimization and launch support.\\n    Quote: As the exclusive PC partner of this game, NVIDIA is collaborating closely with XBOX and game studio The Coalition to enhance the game\\u2019s PC experience through deep integration with GeForce RTX technologies, performance optimization and launch support.\\n- e372 [party_statement; Jakarta Globe; original source Airlangga Hartarto, Indonesia\\u2019s Chief Economic Affairs Minister ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Indonesia\\u2019s Chief Economic Affairs Minister Airlangga Hartarto said planned data-center projects, including Batam, add about 1.3 GW of capacity and represent about $15 billion to $20 billion in investment.\\n    Quote: \\\"Indonesia currently has around 580 MW of operational data center capacity. The additional 1.3 GW that is in the pipeline, including the Batam project, represents investments of around $15 billion (Rp 271 trillion) to $20 billion,\\\" Airlangga said.\\n- e376 [rumour; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that NVIDIA more than halved its list of Asian customers authorised to buy AI chips after creating a new compliance-checked whitelist to prevent shipments reaching China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA has more than halved the number of Asian customers authorised to buy its AI chips after creating a new \\u201cwhite list\\u201d of companies that have passed tougher compliance checks aimed at preventing the products from reaching China, the Financial Times reported on Monday (Jul 14).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e337; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e377 [rumour; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times, citing three people familiar with the matter, reported that NVIDIA intensified customer due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan over the past few months.\\n    Quote: Over the past few months, the chipmaker has intensified due diligence in Singapore, Malaysia and Japan, the report added, citing three people familiar with the matter.\\n- e378 [rumour; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that NVIDIA tightened compliance procedures, with staff visiting customers\\u2019 data centres, verifying contracts and interviewing end users.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has tightened compliance procedures following pressure from Washington, the FT said, adding that staff now visit customers\\u2019 data centres, verify contracts and interview end users as part of the checks.\\n- e379 [fact; businesstimes.com.sg; original source US Commerce Department ; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May to curb advanced AI chips reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, citing concern that Blackwell processors may have reached Chinese-linked entities in countries including Malaysia.\\n    Quote: The US Commerce Department issued guidance in May aimed at curbing advanced AI chips from reaching overseas subsidiaries of Chinese companies, highlighting concerns that Nvidia\\u2019s cutting-edge Blackwell processors may have been exported to Chinese-linked entities in countries such as Malaysia despite US restrictions.\\n- e380 [rumour; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Financial Times 2026-07-14; from gnews:dc642adc9738cb72e71bf4cd 2026-07-14] The Financial Times reported that the US Department of Commerce is providing oversight and political backing for the compliance effort.\\n    Quote: The US Department of Commerce is also involved, providing oversight and political backing, the report said.\\n- e381 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Institute of Science Tokyo ; from nvidianews:japans-enterprises-and-startups-build-industry-specialized-ai-with-nvidia-nemotron-open-models 2026-07-15] The Institute of Science Tokyo developed its Swallow family of open foundation models using NVIDIA Nemotron datasets and NeMo.\\n    Quote: Institute of Science Tokyo developed its Swallow family of open foundation models using NVIDIA Nemotron datasets and the NVIDIA NeMo\\u2122 software stack for continual pretraining and post-training.\\n- e382 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Japan\\u2019s Digital Agency ; from nvidianews:japans-enterprises-and-startups-build-industry-specialized-ai-with-nvidia-nemotron-open-models 2026-07-15] Japan\\u2019s Digital Agency selected SB Intuitions\\u2019 Sarashina3 mini model for specialized AI use cases; the model was trained using NVIDIA Nemotron.\\n    Quote: Sarashina3 mini has been selected by Japan\\u2019s Digital Agency for use in specialized AI use cases.\\n- e383 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Stockmark 2026-07-15; from nvidianews:japans-enterprises-and-startups-build-industry-specialized-ai-with-nvidia-nemotron-open-models 2026-07-15] Stockmark released a specialized Japanese-language document-understanding model based on NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano Omni on 2026-07-15.\\n    Quote: Stockmark \\u2019s specialized Japanese-language document-understanding model, released today, is based on the NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano Omni model.\\n- e384 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source avatarin ; from nvidianews:japans-enterprises-and-startups-build-industry-specialized-ai-with-nvidia-nemotron-open-models 2026-07-15] Avatarin is developing Japanese-language speech and reasoning capabilities for enterprise AI agents using NVIDIA Nemotron and NeMo.\\n    Quote: AI and robotics startup avatarin is using NVIDIA Nemotron open models and NVIDIA NeMo to develop Japanese-language speech and reasoning capabilities for enterprise AI agents.\\n- e385 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NTT DATA ; from nvidianews:japans-enterprises-and-startups-build-industry-specialized-ai-with-nvidia-nemotron-open-models 2026-07-15] NTT DATA used NVIDIA Nemotron-Personas-Japan to augment training data for its tsuzumi 2 model.\\n    Quote: NTT DATA, an operating subsidiary of NTT, used NVIDIA Nemotron-Personas-Japan to augment training data for its proprietary tsuzumi 2 model, improving question-answering accuracy and enhancing responses to questions requiring additional knowledge.\\n- e386 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NTT DATA ; from nvidianews:japans-enterprises-and-startups-build-industry-specialized-ai-with-nvidia-nemotron-open-models 2026-07-15] NTT DATA is looking to deploy a multi-agent framework using NVIDIA Agent Toolkit, including Nemotron, for enterprise workflows.\\n    Quote: The company is also looking to deploy a scalable multi-agent framework harnessing NVIDIA Agent Toolkit , including NVIDIA Nemotron, to route tasks to the best models and drive accurate, efficient and autonomous enterprise workflows.\\n- e387 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Hitachi ; from nvidianews:japans-enterprises-and-startups-build-industry-specialized-ai-with-nvidia-nemotron-open-models 2026-07-15] Hitachi is developing physical AI technologies using NVIDIA Nemotron and Cosmos open models alongside its IT and OT domain knowledge.\\n    Quote: Hitachi is developing physical AI technologies to address real-world operational challenges by using NVIDIA Nemotron and NVIDIA Cosmos\\u2122 open models, along with its proprietary information technology (IT) and operational technology (OT) domain knowledge.\\n- e388 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Sakana AI ; from nvidianews:japans-enterprises-and-startups-build-industry-specialized-ai-with-nvidia-nemotron-open-models 2026-07-15] Sakana AI is integrating NVIDIA Nemotron into its Fugu model-orchestration platform, expanding the models it can orchestrate.\\n    Quote: Sakana AI is collaborating with NVIDIA to integrate NVIDIA Nemotron into its Fugu model-orchestration platform, expanding the range of AI models Fugu can intelligently orchestrate to dynamically select the best model for each task in agentic AI workflows.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e404; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e402 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-07-15; from nvblog:jetson-thor-robotics-edge-ai-agent 2026-07-15] NVIDIA introduced its T3000 and T2000 Thor-based modules for robotics and edge AI on 2026-07-15.\\n    Quote: To meet that need, NVIDIA today introduced the T3000 and T2000, new modules based on the NVIDIA Thor architecture that enable mass-market robotics and edge AI applications at scale.\\n- e403 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-07-15; from nvblog:jetson-thor-robotics-edge-ai-agent 2026-07-15] NVIDIA said the Jetson T3000 and T2000 modules are scheduled to become available in Q1 2027.\\n    Quote: The Jetson T3000 and T2000 modules are scheduled to become available in Q1 2027.\\n- e404 [fact; Sakana AI, in its published announcement; original source Sakana AI 2026-07-15; from gnews:68d900bceeb241f931ab1f2e 2026-07-15] Sakana AI announced that it is integrating NVIDIA Nemotron models as specialized agents in its Sakana Fugu system.\\n    Quote: As part of the expanded collaboration, Sakana is integrating Nemotron, an open model family with open weights and tooling, as specialized agents within Sakana Fugu.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e388; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e405 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-15; from gnews:4e8785bda74ec6e3d7abe4ef 2026-07-15] NVIDIA\\u2019s IT and Operations team launched its internal AI Planner program, which the company says supports planning for rack-scale AI infrastructure with over a million components.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s IT and Operations team launched the AI Planner program\\u2014an internal platform powered by NVIDIA\\u00ae cuOpt\\u2122 decision optimization and NVIDIA Nemotron\\u2122 -based AI agents \\u2014that compressed what-if scenario planning from a day to under 10 minutes, delivered a 6x increase in planner productivity, and set a new internal standard for how AI-driven operations can scale without scaling headcount\\u2014all whil\\n- e406 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-15; from gnews:4e8785bda74ec6e3