ility, Toyota will deploy Nvidia's Omniverse to build digital twins of its vehicle assembly lines, where it will be able to virtually model different production methods and optimise efficiency.\\n- e450 [fact; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Toyota Motor Corp 2026-07-16; from gnews:c8b1d2f1a2834005cfe36b36 2026-07-15] Toyota plans to use NVIDIA's Isaac robotics platform and Nemotron large language models to accelerate automotive software development.\\n    Quote: It will also leverage Nvidia's Isaac robotics platform and Nemotron large language models to accelerate automotive software development.\\n- e451 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e7ea83570963898cb3dfbb37 2026-07-15] NVIDIA reported quarterly revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.23%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA posted $81.61 billion in quarterly revenue on 85.23% growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e351; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e456 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e7ea83570963898cb3dfbb37 2026-07-15] NVIDIA guided Q2 revenue to $91.0 billion and reported $119.0 billion in booked supply commitments.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided Q2 revenue to $91.0 billion with $119.0 billion in supply commitments already booked.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e349, e460; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e458 [fact; Gerelyn Terzo; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2e37109213bd9753af2f50e0 2026-07-15] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion; Networking revenue rose 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Nvidia\\u2019s Q1 FY2027 revenue hit $81.615 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center alone contributing $75.246 billion and Networking revenue rising 199% YoY.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same c