 2026-07-16] Keithen Drury said U.S. federal agencies could spend hundreds of billions of dollars on data centers if AI adoption grows, potentially making the government a large Nvidia client; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: However, AI could become so powerful for the federal government and its agencies that it would need to spend hundreds of billions of dollars on data centers like the AI hyperscalers, which could propel the U.S. government into becoming a large client of Nvidia's.\\n- e483 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source DeepSeek 2026-07-07; from gnews:4edc0959d81f2b32d70e47f9 2026-07-16] DeepSeek is developing its own AI chips to reduce its reliance on Nvidia chips; Reuters reported this on July 7, 2026.\\n    Quote: Chinese tech startup DeepSeek is developing its own AI chips to reduce its reliance on Nvidia chips.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e166; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e484 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Richard Windsor, analyst at Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:4edc0959d81f2b32d70e47f9 2026-07-16] Radio Free Mobile analyst Richard Windsor said NVIDIA's AI chip business in China is at zero and will stay there; the item gives no original statement date.\\n    Quote: Windsor noted that Nvidia is \\\"at zero in China and staying there,\\\" referring to Nvidia's already shrinking business in China due to US restrictions on chip exports.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e134; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e485 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Richard Windsor, analyst at Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:4edc0959d81f2b32d70e47f9 2026-07-16] Radio Free Mobile analyst Richard Windsor said DeepSeek has almost zero chance of challenging NVIDIA outside China, citing China's limited access to advanced chip manufacturing and the time and capital needed to design AI chips; the item gives no original statement date.\\n    Quote: Second, Windsor commented that DeepSeek has almost zero chance of challenging Nvidia outside China. Not only is China shut out of the world's most advanced chip manufacturing capabilities, but designing perfect AI chips takes years and requires massive capital.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e134; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e492 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a2bb93d437d80c346c1d80a4 2026-07-16] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61 billion , up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion (+92% YoY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e204; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e501 [fact; Tom's Hardware, reporting NVIDIA's announcement; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-16; from gnews:4cf92ff695f51dbbb675399a 2026-07-16] NVIDIA announced a plan with Japan's Noetra Corp. to build a 140-megawatt AI factory with 27,500 Rubin GPUs and 13,750 Vera CPUs for Japan's FRONTia program; no deployment date was given.\\n    Quote: Nvidia today announced that it's working with Japan's Noetra Corp. to build a 140-megawatt AI factory packing 27,500 Rubin GPUs and 13,750 Vera CPUs, the compute foundation for FRONTia, the Japanese government's state-funded physical AI program.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e466, e504, e534; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e502 [fact; Tom's Hardware, citing Asia Times; original source NEDO 2026-06-30; from gnews:4cf92ff695f51dbbb675399a 2026-07-16] Noetra and AIST won the NEDO tender on June 30 to run FRONTia from fiscal 2026 through fiscal 2030, with \\u00a5387.3 billion in first-year funding and up to \\u00a51 trillion over five years, subject to stage-gate reviews after the first two years.\\n    Quote: Noetra and the national research institute AIST won a NEDO public tender on June 30 to run the FRONTia project from fiscal 2026 through fiscal 2030, with \\u00a5387.3 billion (roughly $2.4 billion) in first-year funding and up to \\u00a51 trillion (roughly $6.1 billion) over five years, Asia Times reported.\\n- e508 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:19d750b9d8c73eecff5a0018 2026-07-16] The author reports NVIDIA Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and Data Center Networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199%.\\n    Quote: None of them are running Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion at 92% YoY growth, or Data Center Networking at $14.8 billion growing 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e201; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e512 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Fireworks ; from gnews:6531767723bdbbe10fb94b8d 2026-07-16] Fireworks said it was generating more than $1 billion in annualized revenue, five times its level the prior year.\\n    Quote: The company, which is backed by Nvidia, is now generating more than $1 billion in annualized revenue, five times more than it had last year.\\n- e513 [fact; CNBC; original source Fireworks ; from gnews:6531767723bdbbe10fb94b8d 2026-07-16] Fireworks raised $1.5 billion at a $17.5 billion valuation; NVIDIA is among the investors in the round.\\n    Quote: Fireworks, a startup whose cloud service runs open-source AI models for software developers, has raised $1.5 billion at a $17.5 billion valuation.\\n- e514 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Lin Qiao, Fireworks CEO ; from gnews:6531767723bdbbe10fb94b8d 2026-07-16] Fireworks CEO Lin Qiao said the service handled 40 trillion AI tokens per day.\\n    Quote: Fireworks now handles 40 trillion AI tokens per day, Qiao said.\\n- e515 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source Fireworks ; from gnews:6531767723bdbbe10fb94b8d 2026-07-16] Fireworks plans to use proceeds from its new financing to obtain more GPUs and hire more technologists.\\n    Quote: The new money will also help Fireworks obtain more GPUs and hire more technologists.\\n- e534 [party_statement; AFP; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2e9d5650d9e525482062cc00 2026-07-16] NVIDIA said it would sell 27,500 Rubin-series AI chips to Noetra for a government-supported robotics AI-model project.\\n    Quote: Nvidia also said Thursday it would sell 27,500 AI chips from its cutting-edge Rubin series to Noetra, a new consortium of firms including SoftBank and Sony, for a government-supported project to develop a homemade AI model for robotics.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e501; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e537 [fact; NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-16; from gnews:4a689c7ec59054514716a14e 2026-07-16] NVIDIA announced it is working with Noetra to launch a Japan AI factory using 13,750 Vera CPUs and 27,500 Rubin GPUs; the announcement gave no launch date.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA today announced it is working with Noetra Corp. to launch an NVIDIA Vera Rubin AI factory with 13,750 NVIDIA Vera CPUs and 27,500 NVIDIA Rubin GPUs for national physical AI.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e466; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e538 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-16; from gnews:4a689c7ec59054514716a14e 2026-07-16] NVIDIA said the planned Noetra AI factory will deliver 140 megawatts of data-center capacity using its Vera Rubin DSX architecture and related networking and DPU products.\\n    Quote: Built on the NVIDIA Vera Rubin DSX AI factory architecture, the AI factory will deliver 140 megawatts of data center capacity combined with the NVIDIA Spectrum-X Ethernet networking platform, NVIDIA BlueField \\u00ae DPUs, and tightly codesigned silicon, systems and software