up 92%\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e279; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e550 [fact; 247Wallst author Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2b5982d17c88b8e7433e1e15 2026-07-16] NVIDIA networking revenue grew 199% year over year in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: with networking alone up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e458; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e552 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:0e5b33a0b98c921c5e5db08b 2026-07-16] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92% year over year, in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s Data Center segment reached $75.25 billion, up 92% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e352; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e556 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source TSMC ; from gnews:0e5b33a0b98c921c5e5db08b 2026-07-16] TSMC's first-half 2026 revenue was up 35.6% year over year.\\n    Quote: First-half 2026 revenue is already up 35.6% year over year.\\n- e557 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source TSMC ; from gnews:0e5b33a0b98c921c5e5db08b 2026-07-16] TSMC's June 2026 revenue grew 67.9% year over year.\\n    Quote: The June revenue report grew 67.9%\\n- e558 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source TSMC ; from gnews:0e5b33a0b98c921c5e5db08b 2026-07-16] TSMC plans capital expenditures of $52 billion to $56 billion in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: TSMC plans $52 billion to $56 billion in 2026 capex.\\n- e559 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source TSMC ; from gnews:0e5b33a0b98c921c5e5db08b 2026-07-16] TSMC's full-year 2026 outlook was for near 30% revenue growth in U.S. dollars, dependent on 3nm and 2nm ramps holding through the second half.\\n    Quote: TSMC\\u2019s full-year 2026 outlook of near 30% USD 