trillion tokens of real-world usage.\\n    Quote: across 100 trillion tokens of real-world usage, OpenRouter\\u2019s State of AI report found that average prompt tokens per request grew roughly fourfold\\n- e2313 [third_party_view; NVIDIA Technical Blog; original source OpenRouter\\u2019s State of AI report ; from gnews:7606d2313168061b01996797 2026-08-24] OpenRouter\\u2019s State of AI report found that a single agentic request consumes 15 times the tokens of an ordinary chat request.\\n    Quote: single agentic requests consume 15 times the tokens of ordinary chat.\\n- e2314 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source OpenAI and Meta ; from gnews:067169e131df734d99650ce4 2026-08-24] OpenAI and Meta committed to massive deployments of AMD Instinct GPUs, strengthening AMD\\u2019s position as an alternative to Nvidia.\\n    Quote: OpenAI and Meta have committed to massive deployments of AMD Instinct GPUs, helping validate the company as the clearest large-scale alternative to Nvidia Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ).\\n- e2315 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source AMD ; from gnews:067169e131df734d99650ce4 2026-08-24] AMD issued OpenAI and Meta warrants for up to 160 million shares each at $0.01 per share, or 320 million potential shares combined, to induce supply agreements.\\n    Quote: AMD issued OpenAI and Meta warrants covering up to 160 million shares each at an exercise price of $0.01. Together, that is 320 million potential shares, equal to nearly 20% of AMD's roughly 1.63 billion shares outstanding. AMD's own OpenAI filing described the warrant as a \\\"material inducement\\\" for entering the supply agreement.\\n- e2316 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Morgan Stanley analyst Joseph Moore 2026-08-05; from gnews:067169e131df734d99650ce4 2026-08-24] Morgan Stanley analyst Joseph Moore estimated on August 5 that AMD was effectively issuing more than $15 billion of warrants for each $15 billion to $20 billion of OpenAI- and Meta-related revenue, potentially eliminating the GPU business\\u2019s profitability if treated as a cash expense.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley analyst Joseph Moore focused on that cost in an August 5 note. He estimates AMD is effectively issuing more than $15 billion of warrants for every $15 billion to $20 billion of revenue tied to OpenAI and Meta. If the economic value of those warrants were treated like a cash expense, Moore argued, the profitability of that GPU business could disappear.\\n- e2317 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source AMD ; from gnews:067169e131df734d99650ce4 2026-08-24] AMD reported second-quarter revenue of $11.5 billion, up 50% year over year.\\n    Quote: Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) reported second-quarter revenue of $11.5 billion, up 50% year over year,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1446; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2318 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source AMD ; from gnews:067169e131df734d99650ce4 2026-08-24] AMD reported second-quarter Data Center revenue of $6.7 billion, more than double the year-earlier period.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue more than doubled to $6.7 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1447, e2478; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2319 [rumour; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Unnamed sources cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:ee7e42e28c5cf342934099bd 2026-08-24] Bloomberg reported that NVIDIA customers were told AI systems containing Grace Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips would become more expensive when shipments begin early next year, with increases varying by chip generation and memory configuration.\\n    Quote: Some of Nvidia's largest customers have been told that systems containing Grace Blackwell and next-generation Vera Rubin chips will become more expensive when shipments begin early next year, Bloomberg reported. The increases will vary depending on the chip generation a