026-07-16); both are in force: Tom's Hardware reported that Rubin racks were expected to reach volume production in the second half of 2026; NVIDIA said the Noetra facility would support trillion-parameter model training as it expands, suggesting a phased ramp.\\n- e2545 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expected to ship Groq 3 LPX in volume to early adopters later in Q2 FY2027, with Nebius as the first customer.\\n    Quote: We expect to ship Groq 3 LPX in volume later this quarter to early adopters. Nebius will be the first.\\n- e2546 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said sovereign, NeoCloud, and enterprise customers that do not want to design custom silicon were adopting its full-stack AI infrastructure platform.\\n    Quote: Beyond the hyperscalers lies a massive market, anxious to adopt AI, customers with no interest in designing their own custom silicon, NVIDIA is fully proven full stack platform is uniquely suited to help sovereigns, NeoClouds and enterprises build their AI infrastructure\\n- e2547 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expected non-hyperscaler customers to represent roughly half of its Data Center business.\\n    Quote: non-hyperscaler growth, our AICE segment, spanning sovereign, regional NeoClouds, enterprise edge and air-gap data centers will represent roughly half of our data center business.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e604, e3021; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2548 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said global AI venture-capital funding exceeded $400 billion in H1 2026, with roughly 70% spent on compute, versus $265 billion raised in all of 2025.\\n    Quote: Global VC funding in AI, roughly 70% of which is spent on compute exceeded $400 billion in the first half of 2026, surpassing the $265 billion raised in all of 2025.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2639, e3023; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2549 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said nearly 20 AI-native start-ups had annualized revenue run rates above $1 billion, up from 13 in Q4 2025.\\n    Quote: Nearly 20 companies, including Cursor owned by SpaceX, Figma and Together AI now exceed $1 billion in annualized run rate revenue, up from 13 companies in Q4 of last year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3024; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2550 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA sovereign AI business revenue, primarily through regional NeoClouds, grew 35% sequentially and more than tripled year-over-year in Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: In sovereign AI, our business primarily through the regional NeoClouds, grew 35% sequentially and more than tripled year-over-year in Q2.\\n- e2551 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA ; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said it had announced a partnership with Japan's Noetra to build a DSX AI factory for open models and related AI applications.\\n    Quote: Last month, we announced a partnership with Noetra, Japan's national AI company to build an NVIDIA DSX AI factory that will create open models to power AI agents, digital twins, robotics and physical AI applications.\\n- e2558 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said OpenAI had committed to substantial infrastructure deployments through 2030, representing approximately 12 GW of existing and planned NVIDIA compute.\\n    Quote: Open AI has committed to substantial deployments of NVIDIA AI infrastructure through 2030. OpenAI's existing and planned commitments represent approximately 12 gigawatts of NVIDIA compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1947, e2743; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2560 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expected demand from AI labs for which it planned to use its balance sheet to contribute roughly one-quarter of its business in FY2028.\\n    Quote: For context, we expect demand from the AI labs for which we expect to leverage our balance sheet to contribute toward roughly a quarter of our business next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2821; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2561 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said Hopper 200 shipments to China-based customers were less than 1% of Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue and were made under U.S. government licenses.\\n    Quote: In Q2, we shipped less than 1% of our total data center revenue in Hopper 200 products to customers based in China in accordance with the U.S. government licenses.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2577, e2626, e2749, e3032; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2562 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA's forward outlook included no China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: And given ongoing geopolitical uncertainty, there is no China data center compute revenue in our forward outlook.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2349; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2565 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA's days sales outstanding increased to 60 days, which it attributed to extended payment terms for large investment-grade customer purchases shipping over multiple quarters.\\n    Quote: Days of sales outstanding increased to 60 days, reflecting extended payment terms for large purchases by certain investment-grade customers to be shipped over multiple quarters.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2748; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2567 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expected Vera Rubin to account for approximately 20% of Q3 FY2027 Data Center revenue.\\n    Quote: We see Vera Rubin accounting for about 20% of data center revenue in Q3.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2732; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2572 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said its available supply supported approximately 70% of expected FY2028 growth, while demand was substantially higher.\\n    Quote: we have supply for 70%. We have more supply than 70%, but about 70%. Our demand is much higher than that.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2696, e2739; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2574 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000073:q2fy27cfocommentary.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported second-quarter FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially, driven by the Blackwell Ultra 