ms across three publicly available models.\\n    Quote: OpenAI said Jalape\\u00f1o delivered between 1.5 times and 1.9 times more AI work per watt than selected Nvidia systems across three publicly available models.\\n- e2667 [fact; zacks.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3bf42a544ef77114bed3c232 2026-08-26] NVIDIA's Data Center segment generated $89.00 billion in revenue in the July quarter, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's Data Center business alone accounted for $89.00 billion in revenues for the July quarter, up a cool +117% from this time last year.\\n- e2671 [fact; Benzinga; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:1c1eb52d79237b26874d76c7 2026-08-26] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion in fiscal Q2, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 117% to $89 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2608, e2809; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2676 [third_party_view; Shay Boloor, in an emailed statement to Benzinga; original source Shay Boloor 2026-08-26; from gnews:1c1eb52d79237b26874d76c7 2026-08-26] Shay Boloor cited NVIDIA hyperscale revenue of $49 billion and ACIE revenue of $40 billion.\\n    Quote: hyperscale revenue reached $49 billion, while ACIE revenue climbed to $40 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2534; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2679 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:fb2b8382af5aeddeba456594 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reportedly told key customers that servers built with its AI chips will cost more than 15% more starting early 2027.\\n    Quote: According to Bloomberg , Nvidia has told its key customers that servers built with its AI chips will cost more than 15% more starting early next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2279; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2680 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source barchart.com 2026-08-26; from gnews:fb2b8382af5aeddeba456594 2026-08-26] The article reports that DRAM manufacturers\\u2019 output is not keeping pace with current demand, pushing memory prices higher and giving Micron and peers near-term pricing power.\\n    Quote: Even as DRAM manufacturers expand output, they can't keep pace with current demand. The demand-supply gap has pushed memory prices higher while offering Micron and its peers near-term pricing power.\\n- e2681 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:fb2b8382af5aeddeba456594 2026-08-26] NVIDIA raised prices on its gaming graphics cards, with some models increasing by as much as 39%.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has also raised prices on its gaming graphics cards, with some models climbing as much as 39%.\\n- e2682 [rumour; barchart.com; original source Contract server builders for Microsoft, Google, and Oracle ; from gnews:fb2b8382af5aeddeba456594 2026-08-26] Contract server builders for Microsoft, Google, and Oracle reportedly told their customers that server price hikes are coming.\\n    Quote: Companies that build servers under contract for giants like Microsoft (MSFT), Alphabet's Google (GOOGL) (GOOG), and Oracle (ORCL) have reportedly told their own customers about the coming price hikes.\\n- e2685 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:fb2b8382af5aeddeba456594 2026-08-26] NVIDIA's data center networking business revenue grew 199% year over year to nearly $15 billion last quarter.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's data center networking business, which connects thousands of chips so they can act as one giant computer, grew 199% year over year to nearly $15 billion last quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e765, e2765, e2767; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2686 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress 2026-06-04; from gnews:fb2b8382af5aeddeba456594 2026-08-26] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said cloud providers continue to earn strong returns from older Hopper systems, giving them little reason to leave NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: She told the Bank of America audience that new data centers are being built for maximum efficiency, and that older systems like Nvidia's Hopper are still earning strong returns for cloud providers, which gives them little reason to walk away from Nvidia.\\n- e2693 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:a9297b78ac70557679490c59 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q2 total revenue of $96.2 billion, more than double year over year, and Data Center revenue of $89 billion, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal 2027 second quarter, the company reported $96.2 billion in quarterly revenue, more than double a year earlier, while data center revenue climbed 117% to $89 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2607, e2724, e2751, e2784, e2804, e2847, e2968; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2703 [third_party_view; Insider Monkey author; original source Insider Monkey author 2026-08-26; from gnews:0b5bf56eda65c4b0497f599e 2026-08-26] AI compute demand across Blackstone's portfolio companies had surged sevenfold in 2026, according to the article.\\n    Quote: Blackstone Inc. (NYSE:BX) gets a front-row seat to structuring what its president calls a new financeable asset class at a moment when AI compute demand across Blackstone's portfolio companies has already surged sevenfold this year.\\n- e2713 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:58da18a5e0a271a50e9bbdaf 2026-08-26] Hyperscalers accounted for about 54% of NVIDIA Data Center revenue in fiscal 2027 Q2; AI clouds, industrial companies, and enterprise accounted for the remainder.\\n    Quote: In the second quarter, about 54% of Nvidia's data center revenue came from hyperscalers , with the remainder from AI clouds, industrial companies, and enterprise (ACIE).\\n- e2724 [fact; MarketBeat; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:7dfab0010a8ac15786f05387 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 FY2027 total revenue of $96 billion and Data Center revenue of $89 billion; total revenue was more than double the prior year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 revenue of $96 billion, more than double the prior year, with data center revenue reaching $89 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2693; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2726 [fact; MarketBeat; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:7dfab0010a8ac15786f05387 2026-08-26] NVIDIA Data Center revenue increased 18% sequentially to $89 billion in fiscal Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue rose 18% sequentially to $89 billion in the second quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2533, e2946; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2727 [fact; MarketBeat; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:7dfab0010a8ac15786f05387 2026-08-26] NVIDIA revenue from hyperscale customers was $49 billion in fiscal Q2 FY2027, up 13% sequentially, driven by Blackwell demand.\\n    Quote: Revenue from hyperscale customers was $49 billion, up 13% from the prior quarter, driven by demand for Blackwell products.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2534, e3022; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2729 [fact; MarketBeat; original source Amazon Web Services 2026-08-26; from gnews:7dfab0010a8ac15786f05387 2026-08-26] AWS plans to deploy an additional 2 million NVIDIA GPUs from Q2 FY2027 through Q2 FY2029 under an expanded partnership.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA announced an expanded partnership with Amazon Web Services under which AWS plans to deploy an additional 2 million NVIDIA GPUs beginning in the current quarter through the second quarter of fiscal 2029.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matc