to use an additional 2 million of Nvidia\\u2019s graphics processing units (GPUs) across its infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2789, e2838, e2902; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2809 [fact; Sean Williams, The Motley Fool; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3f8674295406cbdcfd6396e7 2026-08-26] NVIDIA Data Center revenue grew 117% year over year in fiscal Q2 2027.\\n    Quote: the data center segment leading the way (117% year-over-year revenue growth)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2671; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2838 [fact; techcrunch.com; original source Amazon and NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] Amazon and NVIDIA announced an expanded partnership that adds an order for 2 million NVIDIA GPUs for Amazon data centers.\\n    Quote: The two companies announced Wednesday an expanded partnership that includes a deal to add another 2 million Nvidia GPU chips to Amazon\\u2019s data centers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2806; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2839 [fact; techcrunch.com; original source Amazon and NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] Amazon\\u2019s newly announced 2-million-GPU order includes Blackwell Ultra, Rubin and Rubin Ultra GPUs, with delivery to AWS data centers planned for 2027 and 2028.\\n    Quote: These GPUs, which are designed to handle the heavy compute demands of training and running AI models, include Nvidia Blackwell Ultra, Rubin, and Rubin Ultra GPUs. The chips will head to Amazon Web Services\\u2019 data centers in 2027 and 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2510, e2894, e2897; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2840 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said demand for the more than 1 million GPUs Amazon had previously agreed to deploy exceeded expectations.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said in a statement that since then, \\u201cdemand has exceeded those expectations.\\u201d\\n- e2841 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said its networking hardware, open models, CPUs, data-processing software and robotics platform will be integrated across AWS.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said Wednesday that its technology, including the networking hardware that connects thousands of GPUs into one system, as well as its open models, CPUs, data processing software, and robotics platform, will also be integrated across AWS.\\n- e2842 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source Amazon and NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] Amazon and NVIDIA said demand from startups, enterprises, AI labs and governments influenced their decision to expand their partnership.\\n    Quote: The companies said \\u201csurging demand\\u201d from startups, enterprises, AI labs, and even governments influenced the decision to work more closely.\\n- e2843 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source Peter DeSantis, Amazon AI chief ; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] Amazon AI chief Peter DeSantis said AWS is in talks to sell its Trainium chips, alternatives to NVIDIA H100 and Blackwell GPUs, to other companies for data-center use.\\n    Quote: Amazon\\u2019s AI chief, Peter DeSantis, has said that AWS is in talks to sell its Trainium chips \\u2014 which are a direct alternative to Nvidia\\u2019s H100 or Blackwell chips for deep learning workloads \\u2014 to other companies for use in data centers.\\n- e2844 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] Amazon reported that its custom-chip business exceeded a $25 billion annualized revenue run rate, driven by $225 billion in total commitments from AI labs including Anthropic and OpenAI.\\n    Quote: Amazon has said its custom chip business is growing, noting on its last earnings call that it crossed a $25 billion annualized revenue run rate, driven by $225 billion in total commitments from AI labs like Anthropic and OpenAI.\\n- e2845 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said Amazon plans to adopt NVIDIA\\u2019s Omniverse, Cosmos, Isaac and Jetson physical-AI stack for its warehouse robot fleet.\\n    Quote: Kress said Amazon plans to adopt Nvidia\\u2019s full physical AI stack to power its fleet of robots. The stack includes Omniverse (its simulation and digital twin platform); Cosmos (its world model platform); Isaac (its robotics development platform); and Jetson (computing hardware for robots and edge AI).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2514; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2846 [fact; techcrunch.com; original source Amazon and NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] AWS plans to serve NVIDIA\\u2019s Nemotron open-model family through Amazon Bedrock and SageMaker.\\n    Quote: On the enterprise side, AWS will serve Nvidia\\u2019s Nemotron family of open models on Amazon Bedrock, its managed foundation model platform, and SageMaker, its managed cloud service.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2638; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2847 [fact; techcrunch.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported second-quarter total sales of $96.2 billion and Data Center revenue of $89 billion, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: Nvidia also reported Wednesday that it recorded sales of $96.2 billion for the second quarter, beating analyst estimates. Data center revenue made up the majority of Nvidia\\u2019s sales for the quarter at $89 billion, up 117% from a year ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2693, e2866, e2886; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2848 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided to third-quarter revenue of $108 billion, with some revenue expected from Rubin GPUs.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said it expects revenue to reach $108 billion in the third quarter, some of which will come from its next-gen Rubin GPUs.\\n- e2852 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI was generating profitable tokens and that more compute could generate more profitable tokens and service profits.\\n    Quote: \\u201cAI is generating profitable tokens \\u2026 If we had more compute, we could generate more profitable tokens, which results in more profit for all of the services. This is the exact phase where we\\u2019re at, which is the reason why everybody\\u2019s leaning in.\\u201d\\n- e2855 [fact; theguardian.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:75ddfd001a59ace54148b344 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported second-quarter Data Center segment revenue of $89 billion, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company saw $89bn in datacenter revenue in the second quarter, a closely watched metric that likewise rose 117% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2804, e3018; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2861 [third_party_view; uk.finance.yahoo.com; original source The article's unnamed forecasters ; from gnews:ae63ad24d55f2e0d72343267 2026-08-26] Analysts forecast NVIDIA Data Center revenue of about $85.7 billion for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: Data cen