inion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3018; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e3032 [fact; Insider Monkey; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ef1c09ba4c3333679aa5e869 2026-08-27] NVIDIA's shipments of older Hopper Data Center products to China accounted for less than 1% of Data Center revenue in the latest quarter.\\n    Quote: Shipments of older Hopper Data Center products to China accounted for less than 1% of Data Center revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2561; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e3034 [fact; Insider Monkey; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ef1c09ba4c3333679aa5e869 2026-08-27] NVIDIA's fiscal Q2 hyperscale revenue was $48.7 billion, up 102% year over year and 13% sequentially.\\n    Quote: Hyperscale revenue reached $48.7 billion, up 102% from a year earlier and 13% sequentially.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3022; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e3035 [fact; Insider Monkey; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ef1c09ba4c3333679aa5e869 2026-08-27] NVIDIA's fiscal Q2 ACIE revenue was $40.3 billion, up 138% year over year and 25% sequentially.\\n    Quote: Revenue from AI clouds, industrial and enterprise customers, or ACIE, increased 138% year over year and 25% sequentially to $40.3 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2537; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e3036 [fact; Insider Monkey; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ef1c09ba4c3333679aa5e869 2026-08-27] ACIE represented roughly 45% of NVIDIA's Data Center revenue in fiscal Q2.\\n    Quote: ACIE now represents roughly 45% of Data Center revenue.\\n- e3042 [fact; Insider Monkey; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ef1c09ba4c3333679aa5e869 2026-08-27] Hyperscalers generated about 55% of NVIDIA's Data Center revenue in the latest quarter.\\n    Quote: Hyperscalers