DIA report for FY2027?: now rung 2 Bullish, judged 2026-08-27\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: LSEG FY2027 revenue estimate: $396 billion, on rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).\n    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): About $407 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2 plus the $108 billion Q3 guidance midpoint, then approximately $121.3 billion for Q4 by carrying forward Q3’s 12.3% sequential growth.\n    Reasons (excerpt): The market reference is LSEG’s $396 billion FY2027 estimate, which sits on rung 3. The reported Q1 and Q2 totals plus Q3 guidance, with Q4 modeled by carrying forward Q3’s sequential growth, imply about $407 billion. That crosses the $400 billion boundary into rung 2 but remains below $450 b\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 3; reasons: The market reference is about $364 billion of FY2027 Data Center revenue: the dependent thesis’s $396 billion FY2027 total-revenue estimate multiplied by NVIDIA’s reported 92% Q1 Data Center mix. That is rung 3. The reported Q2 Data Center revenue was $89 billion on $96.2 billion total revenue, a 92.5% mix. Applying that mix to the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guidance implies about $99.9 billion of Q3 Data Center revenue; carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2-to-Q3 total-revenue guidance implies about $112.2 billion in Q4. With Q1 at $75.25 billion, tha\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
