{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import sqlite3,re,pathlib\nbase=pathlib.Path(\\\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad\\\")\nimport json\nfor a,ids in [(\\\"old-1\\\",[354,978,1142,1208,3464,4163]),(\\\"old-2\\\",[7402,8322]),(\\\"old-3\\\",[4101,5195,5369]),(\\\"linked-1\\\",[8752,8753,8756,8759,8763,8766,8761,8765,8768,8769,8770,8775,8842]),(\\\"control-1\\\",[8926])]:\n p=pathlib.Path(f\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/{a}/prod\\\") if a.startswith(\\\"old\\\") else base/(a+\\\"-copy\\\")\n cn=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\"+str(p/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\")+\\\"?mode=ro\\\",uri=True)\n vx=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\"+str(p/\\\"views.sqlite\\\")+\\\"?mode=ro\\\",uri=True)\n for id in ids:\n  row=cn.execute(\\\"select answer_json,input_tokens,cost_usd from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(id,)).fetchone()\n  j,ti,co=row\n  ans=json.loads(j)\n  v=vx.execute(\\\"select view_id,publication_day,rung,cited_views_json from judgements where call_id=?\\\",(id,)).fetchone()\n  print(a,id,v,ti,co)\n  if id in [8756,8752,8770]: print(ans[\\\"reasons\\\"])\nfor old,new in [\n (\\\"A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand.\\\", \\\"Discount unshipped product targets unless the evidence shows volume in hand.\\\"),\n (\\\"; a component cannot exceed its whole.\\\",\\\".\\\"),\n (\\\"compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\\\",\\\"compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one. Adjust a total only by the change supported against its assumptions for the part. Sum disjoint parts on a common basis.\\\")]:\n print(len(old), len(new), len(new)-len(old))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import sqlite3,re,pathlib\nbase=pathlib.Path(\\\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad\\\")\nimport json\nfor a,ids in [(\\\"old-1\\\",[354,978,1142,1208,3464,4163]),(\\\"old-2\\\",[7402,8322]),(\\\"old-3\\\",[4101,5195,5369]),(\\\"linked-1\\\",[8752,8753,8756,8759,8763,8766,8761,8765,8768,8769,8770,8775,8842]),(\\\"control-1\\\",[8926])]:\n p=pathlib.Path(f\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/{a}/prod\\\") if a.startswith(\\\"old\\\") else base/(a+\\\"-copy\\\")\n cn=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\"+str(p/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\")+\\\"?mode=ro\\\",uri=True)\n vx=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\"+str(p/\\\"views.sqlite\\\")+\\\"?mode=ro\\\",uri=True)\n for id in ids:\n  row=cn.execute(\\\"select answer_json,input_tokens,cost_usd from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(id,)).fetchone()\n  j,ti,co=row\n  ans=json.loads(j)\n  v=vx.execute(\\\"select view_id,publication_day,rung,cited_views_json from judgements where call_id=?\\\",(id,)).fetchone()\n  print(a,id,v,ti,co)\n  if id in [8756,8752,8770]: print(ans[\\\"reasons\\\"])\nfor old,new in [\n (\\\"A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand.\\\", \\\"Discount unshipped product targets unless the evidence shows volume in hand.\\\"),\n (\\\"; a component cannot exceed its whole.\\\",\\\".\\\"),\n (\\\"compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\\\",\\\"compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one. Adjust a total only by the change supported against its assumptions for the part. Sum disjoint parts on a common basis.\\\")]:\n print(len(old), len(new), len(new)-len(old))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1 354 ('v4', '2026-07-07', 2, '[]') 12698 0.002594\nold-1 978 ('v4', '2026-07-15', 1, '[]') 27461 0.004467\nold-1 1142 ('v4', '2026-07-16', 1, '[]') 34035 0.004782\nold-1 1208 ('v4', '2026-07-17', 1, '[]') 30354 0.004495\nold-1 3464 ('v4', '2026-08-14', 1, '[]') 25137 0.004472\nold-1 4163 ('v4', '2026-08-21', 1, '[]') 21473 0.004728\nold-2 7402 ('v16', '2026-09-10', 1, '[]') 6289 0.002843\nold-2 8322 ('v16', '2026-09-17', 1, '[]') 6716 0.003641\nold-3 4101 ('v3', '2026-08-20', 1, '[]') 20195 0.003128\nold-3 5195 ('v3', '2026-08-26', 1, '[]') 43737 0.005729\nold-3 5369 ('v3', '2026-08-27', 1, '[]') 49465 0.006832\nlinked-1 8752 ('v14', '2026-07-14', 3, '[\"v8\"]') 11706 0.002358\nThe market reference is Bloomberg's $393 billion FY2027 projection, which sits in rung 3; the separate description of Wall Street expectations as “well over $300 billion” is too broad to place more precisely. Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion followed by Q2 guidance of $91 billion implies about 11.5% sequential growth; carrying that guided growth forward gives roughly $101.5 billion in Q3 and $113.2 billion in Q4, or about $387 billion for FY2027. That is below the $400 billion boundary and remains in rung 3. The disclosed AWS deployment plan and hyperscaler spending outlook support demand, while the HBM ramp slowdown and tighter China-related controls weigh the other way; neither supplies a quantified FY2027 revenue adjustment sufficient to cross a rung boundary. NVIDIA's $18–19 billion stand-alone CPU sales forecast is included within total revenue, not added on top, and is consistent with the whole-revenue estimate.\nlinked-1 8753 ('v9', '2026-07-14', 3, '[\"v14\"]') 13741 0.002954\nlinked-1 8756 ('v14', '2026-07-15', 2, '[\"v8\"]') 15485 0.003605\nBloomberg's $393 billion projection is the clearest market reference and sits in rung 3; the separate “well over $300 billion” expectation is too broad to locate more precisely. The Q1 result and Q2 guidance imply a roughly $387 billion FY2027 run-rate if Q2's sequential growth carries through Q3 and Q4, below the $400 billion boundary. Adding the dependency's roughly $19.5 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU forecast, which is distinct from the existing revenue run-rate, gives about $407 billion and crosses into rung 2. This remains a forecast rather than an established result: the AWS deployment plan and $119 billion in supply-related commitments are not specified as FY2027 revenue, while HBM ramp constraints and custom-chip alternatives are downside risks.\nlinked-1 8759 ('v14', '2026-07-16', 2, '[\"v8\"]') 19753 0.003362\nlinked-1 8763 ('v14', '2026-07-17', 2, '[\"v8\"]') 19529 0.003671\nlinked-1 8766 ('v14', '2026-07-18', 2, '[\"v8\"]') 17895 0.002892\nlinked-1 8761 ('v9', '2026-07-16', 3, '[\"v14\"]') 18176 0.003376\nlinked-1 8765 ('v9', '2026-07-17', 3, '[\"v14\"]') 17990 0.003793\nlinked-1 8768 ('v9', '2026-07-18', 3, '[\"v14\"]') 17405 0.003354\nlinked-1 8769 ('v9', '2026-07-19', 3, '[\"v14\"]') 14239 0.00366\nlinked-1 8770 ('v14', '2026-07-20', 3, '[\"v8\"]') 16237 0.002972\nThe market reference is Bloomberg's $393 billion FY2027 projection, which is in rung 3. Q1 revenue of $81.615 billion followed by Q2 guidance of $91 billion implies 11.5% sequential growth; carrying that rate through Q3 and Q4 implies about $387 billion for FY2027, still in rung 3 and below the $400 billion boundary. The approximately $19 billion stand-alone CPU forecast is a component of total revenue, not an amount to add to this company-wide run-rate. Strong orders and the UAE export easing support the outlook, while the stated China exclusion and HBM supply concerns weigh against it; none provides a quantified FY2027 adjustment that moves the run-rate across a rung boundary.\nlinked-1 8775 ('v9', '2026-07-21', 3, '[\"v14\"]') 13124 0.003944\nlinked-1 8842 ('v9', '2026-08-08', 3, '[\"v14\"]') 15194 0.003149\ncontrol-1 8926 ('v16', '2026-09-05', 1, '[]') 7399 0.002804\n139 76 -63\n38 1 -37\n66 186 120\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'target for a product|discounted by default|volume in hand|accounting identities|carries the guided growth|confirmed delay or cancellation' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/prd/06-views.md | head -32\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'target for a product|discounted by default|volume in hand|accounting identities|carries the guided growth|confirmed delay or cancellation' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/prd/06-views.md | head -32\"","aggregated_output":"docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3053:- Decided, the analyst's rule: (1) the rung is a forecast, the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. (2) The reference is what the market expects: consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline; a consensus or guidance figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and, once other evidence has arrived, is never the reason to stay. (3) The judge derives the outcome the evidence implies (reported figures and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it), checks it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole; a figure spanning several periods or products gives the question only its share), compares it with the rung boundaries and moves when it crosses one. (4) Weight follows tier and novelty: fact fixes what is known; party statements are the strongest forecast input; third-party views and rumours move the forecast in proportion to their specificity; a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing. (5) The answer states `reference` and `implied_outcome` as required fields from `judging-v6` (`judging.schema_for`; code refuses an empty one; stored beside the rung in `judgements.reference` / `implied_outcome`; a ledger written before v6 gains the columns at its first write), so the D3 stance gold can read the reasoning, not only the rung. Written where the judgement is specified: PRD 06 State rules (`docs/system-design/new-facts.js` STATE_RULES, the generated block) and this record.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3072:- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `poc-v91`; schema and code unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
